hadiths[315]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3330","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: I will come to the gate of Paradise on the Day of Resurrection and ask for it to be opened. The keeper will say: Who are you? I will say: Muhammad. He will say: I have been commanded not to open for anyone before you."
"3331","Anas ibn Malik said: Umm Sulaym had an orphan girl under her care, and she was the mother of Anas. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw the orphan girl and said: ""Is it you? You have grown old; may your old age not increase."" The orphan girl returned to Umm Sulaym weeping. Umm Sulaym said: ""What is the matter with you, my little daughter?"" The girl said: ""The Prophet of Allah ﷺ supplicated against me that my old age may not increase""—or she said: ""my horn."" So Umm Sulaym went out hastily, dragging her headscarf, until she met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: ""What is the matter with you, O Umm Sulaym?"" She said: ""O Prophet of Allah! Did you supplicate against my orphan girl?"" He said: ""And what is that, O Umm Sulaym?"" She said: ""She claims that you supplicated that her old age may not increase and her horn may not increase."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed, then said: ""O Umm Sulaym! Do you not know that my condition with my Lord is that I stipulated upon my Lord, saying: 'I am only human; I am pleased as humans are pleased, and I get angry as humans get angry. So whichever person I supplicate against from my Ummah with a supplication not befitting for them, make it for him a purification, a zakah, and a means of nearness that brings him close to You on the Day of Resurrection.'"""
"3332","[AI-translation] From Anas, marfu'an: The sign of faith is love for the Ansar, and the sign of hypocrisy is hatred for the Ansar."
"3333","[AI-translation] From Aisha, she said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, became seriously ill, he said to 'Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakr: ""Bring me a shoulder blade or a board so that I may write a document for Abu Bakr which will not be disputed."" When 'Abd al-Rahman got up to go, he said: ""Allah and the believers refuse that there should be any dispute against you, O Abu Bakr."
"3334","ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ purchased a camel—or camels—from a Bedouin man for a wisq of tamr al-dhakīrah (and tamr al-dhakīrah is the ʿajwah variety). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned with it to his house and sought the dates but did not find them. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to him and said: ""O servant of Allah! We have bought from you a camel—or camels—for a wisq of tamr al-dhakīrah; we sought it but did not find it."" The Bedouin said: ""Wā ghadrāh!"" (Oh, his treachery!). The people hemmed him in and said: ""May Allah fight you! Does the Messenger of Allah ﷺ act treacherously?"" She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Leave him, for the owner of a right has a say."" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned and said: ""O servant of Allah! We bought your camels, and we thought we had what we named for you; we sought it but did not find it."" The Bedouin said: ""Wā ghadrāh!"" The people fell upon him and said: ""May Allah fight you! Does the Messenger of Allah ﷺ act treacherously?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Leave him, for the owner of a right has a say."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ repeated that two or three times. When he saw that he did not comprehend, he said to a man from his Companions: ""Go to Khawlah bint Ḥakīm ibn Umayyah and say to her: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ says to you: If you have a wisq of tamr al-dhakīrah, lend it to us until we repay it to you, if Allah wills.'"" The man went to her, then returned and said: ""She said: 'Yes, it is with me, O Messenger of Allah! Send someone to collect it.'"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the man: ""Go with it and give him his due."" So he went with it and gave him his due. She said: Then the Bedouin passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was sitting among his Companions and said: ""May Allah reward you with good, for you have fulfilled and given generously."" She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Those are the best of Allah's servants in Allah's sight on the Day of Resurrection: those who fulfill their obligations and give generously."""
"3335","On the authority of Muhammad ibn Umar al-Aslami, with his chains of transmission from a group of the Companions, he said: The hadith of some of them entered into the hadith of others. They said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) sent Abdullah ibn Hudhafah al-Sahmi, who was one of the six, to Kisra (Khosrow) calling him to Islam, and he wrote a letter with him. Abdullah said: I delivered to him the letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family). It was read to him, then he took it and tore it up. When that reached the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family), he said: ""O Allah, tear up his kingdom."" And Kisra wrote to Badhan, his governor over Yemen, saying: ""Send from your side two strong men to this man in the Hijaz, that they may bring me news of him."" So Badhan sent Qahraman and another man, and wrote a letter with them. They arrived in Medina, and they delivered Badhan's letter to the Prophet (peace be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) smiled, and called them to Islam, and their limbs were trembling. He said: ""Return from me today until you come to me tomorrow, that I may inform you of what I intend."" So they came to him the next day, and he said to them: ""Convey to your master that my Lord has killed your lord Kisra this night."""
"3336","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, marfu'an: The two sons of al-'As are believers: Hisham and 'Amr."
"3337","[AI-translation] He, peace be upon him, said: Abu Bakr and 'Umar are the masters of the mature youth among the people of Paradise, from the first to the last. Narrated by a group of the Companions... transmitted."
"3338","[AI-translation] From Jabir bin 'Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: Abu Bakr and 'Umar in this religion are like the status of hearing and sight in the head."
"3339","[AI-translation] Badri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Abu Sufyan bin al-Harith is the best of my family."
"3340","[AI-translation] From Bilal bin Yahya, he said: When 'Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed, they came to Hudhayfah and said: O Abu 'Abdullah! This man has been killed, and the people have differed; so what do you say? He said: ""Prop me up."" So they propped him against the chest of a man, and he said: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: Abu al-Yaqzan is upon the Fitrah; he will not abandon it until he dies or old age touches him."
"3341","[AI-translation] Zuraqi, from his father—and his father was among the people of Badr, and his grandfather was among the people of al-'Aqabah—he said: Jibril came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, and said: ""What do you consider the people of Badr to be among you?"" He said: ""Among the best of the Muslims."" He said: ""And likewise are those of the angels who witnessed it with us."
"3342","[AI-translation] From Anas: Ukaydir of Dumat sent a cloak of fine silk to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, wore it, and the people marveled at it. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Are you amazed by this? By the One in Whose hand is my soul, the handkerchiefs of Sa'd bin Mu'adh in Paradise are better than it."" Then he gifted it to 'Umar. He said: ""O Messenger of Allah! You disliked it, yet you clothe me in it?"" He said: ""O 'Umar! I only sent it to you so that you may send it [as a gift], and thereby obtain wealth; and that was before silk was prohibited."
"3343","On the authority of ʿAmr ibn ʿAbasah: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, who has followed you in this matter?"" He said: ""A free man and a slave."" I said: ""What is Islam?"" He said: ""Good speech and feeding food."" I said: ""What is faith (Īmān)?"" He said: ""Patience and generosity."" I said: ""Which Islam is best?"" He said: ""He from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe."" I said: ""Which faith is best?"" He said: ""Good character."" I said: ""Which prayer is best?"" He said: ""Length of standing (in prayer)."" I said: ""Which emigration (Hijrah) is best?"" He said: ""That you abandon what your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, hates."" I said: ""Then which jihad is best?"" He said: ""He whose horse is hamstrung and his blood is shed."" I said: ""Which hours are best?"" He said: ""The depth of the last part of the night..."""
"3344","[AI-translation] He, peace be upon him, said: ""Be firm, O Hira, for there is none upon you except a Prophet, a Siddiq, or a martyr."" Transmitted in the hadith of......"
"3345","On the authority of Sa'id ibn al-'As, that Aisha, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) — and Muslim and others added: ""and Uthman"" — both narrated to him that Abu Bakr sought permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) while he was reclining on his bed wearing Aisha's garment. He granted permission to Abu Bakr while in that state, so he attended to his need and then left. Then Umar sought permission, so he granted him permission while in that same state, and he attended to his need and then left. Uthman said: ""Then I sought permission, so he sat up and said to Aisha: 'Gather your clothes around you.' So I attended to my need and then left."" Aisha said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Why did I not see you startled for Abu Bakr and Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) as you were startled for Uthman?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Uthman is a man of modesty, and I feared that if I granted him permission while in that state, he would not convey his need to me."""
"3346","[AI-translation] From Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab addressed us at al-Jabiyah and said: Verily, the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, stood among us as I stand among you, and said: Preserve my right regarding my Companions, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then lying will become widespread until a man will testify without being asked to, and swear an oath without being asked to."
"3347","Ibn 'Abbas said: I heard 'Umar ibn al-Khattab say: When 'Abdullah ibn Ubayy died, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was invited to perform the funeral prayer for him. He stood up to do so, and when he stood over him intending to pray, I moved until I stood at his chest and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Upon the enemy of Allah, 'Abdullah ibn Ubayy, who said on such-and-such day such-and-such?"" — enumerating his days. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept smiling until I spoke at length. He said: ""Leave me, O 'Umar! I have been given the choice, and I chose. It has been said (to me): 'Ask forgiveness for them, or do not ask forgiveness for them. Even if you ask forgiveness for them seventy times, Allah will never forgive them' (Al-Tawbah: 80). Had I known that if I increased beyond seventy he would be forgiven, I would have increased."" Then he prayed over him and walked with him, and stood at his grave until he was buried. He said: I was amazed at myself and my boldness toward the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while Allah and His Messenger know best. By Allah, it was only a short while until these two verses were revealed: ""And never pray over any of them who dies, nor stand at his grave. Indeed, they disbelieved in Allah and His Messenger and died while they were defiantly disobedient"" (Al-Tawbah: 84) — to the end of the verse. He said: So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ never prayed over a hypocrite after him, nor stood at his grave, until Allah took him."
"3348","[AI-translation] From Ka'b ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: When you conquer Egypt, treat the Copts well, for they have a covenant and a tie of kinship."
"3349","[AI-translation] He said, peace be upon him: When the sons of Abu al-As reach thirty men, they will make the religion of Allah a means of access, the servants of Allah slaves, and the wealth of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, spoils to be distributed."
"3350","[AI-translation] He said, peace be upon him: When my Companions are mentioned, refrain; and when the stars are mentioned, refrain; and when predestination is mentioned, refrain."
"3351","[AI-translation] From Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah from his father, raised to the Prophet: If the people of al-Sham become corrupt, there is no good in you. A group from my Ummah will continue to be victorious, unharmed by those who abandon them, until the Hour is established."
"3352","[AI-translation] From Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: You have my permission to lift the veil and listen to my voice until I forbid you."
"3353","[AI-translation] From Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: The most merciful of my Ummah towards my Ummah is Abu Bakr; the firmest of them in the matter of Allah is Umar; the most bashful of them is Uthman; the best of them in reciting the Book of Allah is Ubayy ibn Ka'b; the most knowing of them in the laws of inheritance is Zayd ibn Thabit; and the most knowing of them regarding the lawful and unlawful is Mu'adh ibn Jabal. Verily, for every nation there is a trustworthy one, and the trustworthy one of this nation is Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah."
"3354","[AI-translation] From Umm Habibah, from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, he said: I was shown what my Ummah will face after me, and some of them shedding the blood of others, and that was preordained by Allah just as it was preordained for the nations before them. So I asked Him to grant me intercession for them on the Day of Resurrection, and He did so."
"3355","[AI-translation] From Ibn Umar, raised to the Prophet: The most beloved of people to me is Usamah, excluding Fatimah and others."
"3356","From Ḥubbān ibn Wāsiʿ ibn Ḥubbān, from the elders of his people, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ aligned the rows of his Companions on the Day of Badr. In his hand was an arrow with which he was straightening the people. He passed by Sawād ibn Ghaziyya, ally of Banū ʿAdī ibn al-Najjār, who was protruding from the row. He poked him in the stomach with the arrow and said: ""Straighten up, O Sawād."" He said: ""O Messenger of Allah! You have hurt me, and Allah has sent you with justice, so allow me to retaliate."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then exposed his stomach and said: ""Retaliate."" So he embraced him and kissed his stomach. He said: ""What prompted you to do this, O Sawād?"" He said: ""O Messenger of Allah! What you see has befallen me (i.e., the battle is at hand), so I wished that the last contact between me and you would be my skin touching your skin."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated for him with goodness and said to him: ""Straighten up, O Sawād."""
"3357","[AI-translation] From Ali ibn Zayd, he said: Something reached Mus'ab ibn al-Zubayr regarding the leader of the Ansar, and he intended to punish him. Anas ibn Malik entered upon him and said to him: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: Treat the Ansar well — or he said: kindly — Accept from their doer of good and overlook their doer of evil. So Mus'ab threw himself from his couch and pressed his cheek against the carpet and said: The command of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, is upon the head and the eye. So he left him."
"3358","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah, elevated to the Prophet: The fastest of the Arab tribes to perish is Quraysh, and it is near that a woman will pass by the shoe and say, ""This is the shoe of a Qurashi."
"3359","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: Aslam, may Allah grant it peace, and Ghifar, may Allah forgive it. Verily, I did not say it, but Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said it."
"3360","[AI-translation] Narrated Uqbah bin Amir: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him: The most submissive of people and the most faithful is Amr bin Al-Aas."
"3361","[AI-translation] Ansari from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: Aslam, Ghifar, Ashja, Muzainah, Juhainah, and whoever was from Banu Kaab are clients apart from the people, and Allah and His Messenger are their patron."
"3362","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Shihab, mursal: The one I saw most resembling Jibril was Dihyah Al-Kalbi."
"3363","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Dharr who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: The most intense of my nation in love for me are a people who will be or will come after me; one of them would wish that he had given his family and his wealth, and that he had seen me."
"3364","[AI-translation] Narrated Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A letter from a man came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, and he said to Abdullah bin Al-Arqam: ""Answer on my behalf."" So he wrote its reply, then read it to him, and he said: ""You have hit the mark and done well. O Allah, grant him success."" When Umar was appointed, he used to consult him."
"3365","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas bin Malik that a man said: ""O Messenger of Allah, verily so-and-so has a palm tree and I maintain my palm tree by it, so command him to give it to me (it) (so that) I may establish my wall by it."" The Prophet, peace be upon him, said to him: ""Give it to him for a palm tree in Paradise."" But he refused, and Abu Ad-Dahdah came to him and said: ""Sell me your palm tree for my wall."" He said: So he did. He said: Then he came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I have bought the palm tree."
"3366","[AI-translation] Siddiq who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: I was given seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without account, their faces like the moon on the night of the full moon, and their hearts upon the heart of one man. So I asked my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, for more, and He added to me with every one seventy thousand. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: So I saw that that would befall the people of the towns and strike those on the outskirts of the desert."
"3367","[AI-translation] Ashari, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: I was given the openings of speech and its conclusions. We said: ""O Messenger of Allah, teach us from what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has taught you."" So he taught us the Tashahhud."
"3368","[AI-translation] Narrated from 'Ali bin Abi Talib who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""I was given what no one of the prophets was given."" We said: ""O Messenger of Allah! What is it?"" He said: ""I was given victory by terror, I was given the keys of the earth, I was named Ahmad, dust was made a purifier for me, and my nation was made the best of nations."
"3369","[AI-translation] Asqa' who said: The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""I was given the seven long ones (Al-Sab' Al-Tiwal) in place of the Torah, the hundreds (Al-Mi'in) in place of the Psalms, the oft-repeated (Al-Mathani) in place of the Gospel, and I was distinguished by the detailed (Al-Mufassal)."
"3370","[AI-translation] Narrated from Hudhayfah, raised to the Prophet: ""I was given these verses from the end of Al-Baqarah from a treasure beneath the Throne; no prophet before me was given them (and no one after me will be given them)."
"3371","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurayrah who said: He, peace be upon him, said: ""The best of days with Allah is the day of Friday."
"3372","[AI-translation] He, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""Follow the two who come after me from my companions, Abu Bakr and 'Umar, and take guidance from the guidance of 'Ammar, and hold fast to the pledge of Ibn Mas'ud."" Narrated from the hadith of..."
"3373","[AI-translation] Narrated from 'Abdullah bin 'Amr who said: I used to write down everything I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, intending to memorize it. But Quraysh forbade me and said: ""Do you write down everything? The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, is a human being who speaks in anger and pleasure."" So I refrained from writing. I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, and he gestured with his finger to his mouth and said: ""Write, for by the One in Whose Hand my soul is, nothing comes out of it except the truth."
"3374","[AI-translation] The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Shall I not inform you of the best of the houses of the Ansar?"" - or ""the best of the Ansar""? They said: ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""Banu An-Najjar, then those who follow them Banu 'Abd Al-Ashhal, then those who follow them Banu Al-Harith bin Al-Khazraj, then those who follow them Banu Sa'idah."" Then he gestured with his hand, clasping his fingers and then spreading them like an archer with his hands, and said: ""And in all the houses of the Ansar there is good."" It is narrated from the hadith of..."
"3375","[AI-translation] Narrated from Anas bin Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, came out to us and said: ""Verily, for everything there is a resting place and a safeguard, and my resting place and safeguard are the Ansar. So preserve me among them."
"3376","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Qatadah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, saying on the pulpit to the Ansar: ""Verily, the people are my outer garment and the Ansar are my inner garment. If the people were to traverse a valley, and the Ansar were to traverse a mountain pass, I would follow the mountain pass of the Ansar. Were it not for the Hijrah, I would have been a man from the Ansar. So whoever takes charge of the affairs of the Ansar, let him be good to their good-doers and overlook the wrongdoers among them. And whoever frightens them has frightened the one between these two,"" and he pointed to himself, peace be upon him and his family."
"3377","[AI-translation] The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Verily, I absolve myself from the deep friendship of every close friend, and if I were to take a close friend, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend. Your companion is the close friend of Allah."" It is narrated from the hadith of..."
"3378","[AI-translation] Narrated Umm Salamah: That the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, advised at the time of his death, saying: Fear Allah, fear Allah regarding the Copts of Egypt, for you will conquer them, and they will be for you a multitude and helpers in the path of Allah."
"3379","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas bin Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: O Allah, make in al-Madinah twice what You have made in Makkah of blessing."
"3380","[AI-translation] Rahman bin Abi Umayrah al-Muzani from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, that he said regarding Mu'awiyah: O Allah, make him a guide, rightly guided, and guide him, and guide others through him."
"3381","[AI-translation] Narrated Aishah: That the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: O Allah, strengthen Islam through Umar bin al-Khattab specifically."
"3382","[AI-translation] Narrated Hudhayfah who said: I came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, and prayed al-Maghrib with him. When he finished, he prayed, and he did not cease praying until he prayed al-Isha, then he went out. I followed him. He said: Who is this? I said: Hudhayfah. He said: O Allah, forgive Hudhayfah and his mother."
"3383","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: ""When I saw the Prophet (peace be upon him) in a cheerful mood, I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Supplicate to Allah for me.' He said: 'O Allah, forgive Aisha her past and future sins, what she has concealed and what she has made public.' Aisha laughed until her head fell into the lap of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) from laughter. He said: 'Does my supplication please you?' She said: 'And why would your supplication not please me?' He said: 'By Allah, it is my supplication for my Ummah in every prayer.'"""
"3384","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas bin Malik who said: My mother took me to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is your servant, so invoke Allah for him. He said: O Allah, make his wealth and his children abundant, and prolong his life, and forgive him. He said: So my wealth multiplied, and my life grew long until I felt shy of my family, and my fruits ripened, and as for the fourth, meaning forgiveness."
"3385","[AI-translation] Narrated from Anas bin Malik, raised to the Prophet: O Allah, make his wealth and his children abundant, and bless him in what You have given him."
"3386","Abu Huraira said: ""I never saw Hasan without my eyes overflowing with tears. That is because the Prophet (peace be upon him) went out one day and found me in the mosque. He took my hand, and I went with him. He did not speak to me until we reached the market of Banu Qaynuqa'. He walked around in it and looked, then he turned back and I was with him, until we reached the mosque. He sat down and wrapped his garment around his legs, then said: 'Where is Luqa'? Call Luqa' for me.' Hasan came running and fell into his lap. Then he put his hand into his beard. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) opened his mouth and put his mouth into his mouth. Then he said: 'O Allah, I love him, so love him, and love whoever loves him.'"""
"3387","[AI-translation] Bara' who said: I saw the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, and al-Hasan bin Ali on his shoulder, and he was saying: O Allah, I love him, so love him."
"3388","On the authority of ʿĀʾishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Medina, Abū Bakr and Bilāl fell ill. She said: I entered upon them and said: ""O my father! How do you find yourself? And O Bilāl! How do you find yourself?"" She said: Abū Bakr, when the fever seized him, would say:""Every man is struck down among his family,And death is nearer to him than the strap of his sandal.""And Bilāl, when the fever left him, would raise his voice and say—and in a narration of Aḥmad: he would sing, saying:""Would that I knew if I shall spend a nightIn a valley, surrounded by idhkhir and jālil?And shall I one day drink the waters of Majannah?And shall Shāmah and Ṭufayl appear to me?""ʿĀʾishah said: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him, so he said: ""O Allah, make Medina beloved to us as You made Mecca beloved to us, or even more. And make it healthy, and bless for us its ṣāʿ and its mudd. And transfer its fever, and place it in Al-Juḥfah."" (Aḥmad added in a narration: He said: ""So a child would be born in Al-Juḥfah, and would not reach puberty before the fever would strike him down."")"
"3389","[AI-translation] Narrated from Aishah bint Sa'd from her father: That the Prophet, peace be upon him, had food in front of him, and he said: O Allah! bring to this food a servant whom You love and who loves You. So Sa'd (bin Abi Waqqas) appeared."
"3390","[AI-translation] The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: O Allah, teach Mu'awiyah the Book and the reckoning, and protect him from the punishment. Transmitted from the hadith of ....... ( )"
"3391","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas: That he poured water for the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) for ablution at his aunt Maymunah's. When he came out, he said: ""Who placed my ablution water for me?"" She said: ""Your nephew, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""O Allah, grant him understanding in the religion, and teach him the interpretation."
"3392","[AI-translation] Samit, elevated to the Prophet: ""O Allah, whoever wrongs the people of Al-Madinah and frightens them, frighten him, and upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all the people. Neither charity nor ransom will be accepted from him."
"3393","Muhammad ibn Usamah narrated from his father who said: Ja'far, 'Ali, and Zayd ibn Harithah gathered together. Ja'far said: ""I am the most beloved of you to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."" Zayd said: ""I am the most beloved of you to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."" They said: ""Let us go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ask him."" Usamah ibn Zayd said: ""They came seeking permission to enter. He said: 'Go out and see who these people are.' I said: 'This is Ja'far, 'Ali, and Zayd.' He did not mention my father. He said: 'Permit them.' They entered and said: 'Who is most beloved to you?' He said: 'Fatimah.' They said: 'We are asking you about the men.' He said: 'As for you, O Ja'far! Your appearance resembles my appearance and your character resembles my character. You are from me and my tree (lineage). As for you, O 'Ali! You are my brother (khatani) and the father of my children (grandchildren), and I am from you and you are from me. As for you, O Zayd! You are my freed slave (mawla) and from me and to me, and the most beloved of the people to me.'"""
"3394","[AI-translation] From 'Aishah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) mentioned Fatimah. She said: So I spoke, and he said: ""Are you not pleased to be my wife in this world and the Hereafter?"" I said: ""Yes, by Allah!"" He said: ""Then you are my wife in this world and the Hereafter."
"3395","On the authority of Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) was approached, and it was said to him: ""These are the Anṣār, their men and their women, in the mosque weeping!"" He said: ""And what makes them weep?"" It was said: ""They fear that you may die."" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) came out, wearing a cloak wrapped around his shoulders, and on his head was a bandage stained with oil, until he sat on the pulpit—and it was the last gathering in which he sat. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: ""As for what follows! O people, indeed the people will increase and the Anṣār will decrease until they become like salt in food. So whoever among you assumes authority over an affair (of the nation of Muḥammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and is able to) harm or benefit someone therein, let him accept the good of their doers of good and overlook the wrong of their wrongdoers."""
"3396","[AI-translation] Zubayr who said: I heard Jabir saying: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) passed by a man turning over on his back and stomach, so he asked about him. They said: ""He is fasting, O Prophet of Allah."" He called him and ordered him to break his fast, saying: ""Is it not enough for you to be in the path of Allah and with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) that you fast?"
"3397","[AI-translation] He (peace be upon him) said: ""I was commanded to give glad tidings to Khadijah of a house in Paradise of hollow pearls, in which there is no noise nor fatigue."" Transmitted from the hadith of ........."
"3398","On the authority of Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: ""I was commanded [to go to] a village that consumes other villages; they say: Yathrib, and it is Medina. It expels people just as the bellows expels the impurities of iron."" And in another narration from another chain from him, marfu' (attributed to the Prophet), with the wording: ""There will come upon people a time when a man will call his cousin and his relative: 'Come to prosperity, come to prosperity,' but Medina is better for them, if they only knew. And by the One in Whose Hand is my soul! No one leaves it out of aversion to it except that Allah will replace him in it with someone better than him. Verily, Medina is like the bellows: it expels the wicked. The Hour will not be established until Medina expels its wicked, just as the bellows expels the impurities of iron."""
"3399","[AI-translation] Rahman who narrated to him, he said: I entered upon 'Aishah and she said to me: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) used to say to me: ""Your affairs are among what concerns me after me, and none will be patient with you except the patient ones."" Then she said: ""May Allah give your father to drink from the Salsabil of Paradise."" And 'Abdul-Rahman bin 'Awf had gifted them wealth that was sold for forty thousand."
"3400","[AI-translation] From Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) went out and said to his Companions: ""Walk in front of me and leave my back for the angels."
"3401","[AI-translation] Malik bin 'Umayr who said: 'Umar bin Al-Khattab appointed Abu 'Ubaydah bin Al-Jarrah over Al-Sham, and dismissed Khalid bin Al-Walid. So Khalid bin Al-Walid said: ""The trustee of this Ummah has been sent over you. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: 'The trustee of this Ummah is Abu 'Ubaydah bin Al-Jarrah.'"" Abu 'Ubaydah said: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: 'Khalid is a sword from the swords of Allah; what an excellent youth of the clan he is.'"
"3402","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah bin Zayd from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) who said: ""Indeed, Ibrahim made Makkah sacred and supplicated for it, and I have made Al-Madinah sacred just as Ibrahim made Makkah sacred, and I supplicated for it in its mudd and sa' just as Ibrahim supplicated for Makkah."
"3403","[AI-translation] That 'Aishah said: ""Do not tell your wives that I chose you."" So the Prophet (peace be upon him) said to her: ""Indeed, Allah sent me as a conveyor and did not send me as one who causes hardship."
"3404","[AI-translation] Asqa', may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: Allah chose Kinanah from the descendants of Isma'il, and He chose Quraysh from Kinanah, and He chose Banu Hashim from Quraysh, and He chose me from Banu Hashim."
"3405","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, marfu'an: Allah, Mighty and Majestic (in one wording: Perhaps Allah), looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do as you wish, for I have forgiven you."
"3406","[AI-translation] Ash'ari, who heard the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, say: ""Allah has protected my Ummah from uniting upon misguidance."
"3407","[AI-translation] Ash'ari, from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, who said: ""Allah looks down on the night of the middle of Sha'ban and forgives all of His creation, except for a polytheist or one who harbors enmity."
"3408","[AI-translation] From Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, used to set up a pulpit for Hassan in the mosque, upon which he would stand, boasting on behalf of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family—or he said: defending the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family. And the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, would say: ""Allah supports Hassan with the Holy Spirit as long as he defends or boasts on behalf of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family."
"3409","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""People from my Ummah will come after me; one of them would wish to trade his family and wealth to see me."
"3410","[AI-translation] From Anas ibn Malik: The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, went out one day with his head bandaged. The children of the Ansar and their servants, who were the reserves of the Ansar at that time, met him. He said: ""By the One in Whose hand is my soul, I love you,"" twice or thrice. Then he said: ""The Ansar have fulfilled what was incumbent upon them, and what remains is incumbent upon you. So be good to those of them who do good, and overlook those who do wrong."
"3411","[AI-translation] Rahman ibn Abi Nu'm, who said: A man asked Ibn Umar—and I was sitting—about the blood of a mosquito that gets on a garment. He said to him: ""Where are you from?"" He said: ""From the people of Iraq."" Ibn Umar said: ""Look at this one! He asks about the blood of a mosquito, while they have killed the son of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family! I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: Al-Hasan and Al-Husayn are my two sweet basils from this world."
"3412","[AI-translation] Ash'ari, marfu'an: ""The best of the servants of Allah from this Ummah are those who, when they are seen, Allah is remembered. And the worst of the servants of Allah from this Ummah are those who walk about with calumny, separating between the beloved, and seeking to bring trouble upon the innocent."
"3413","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, who said: A man from Banu Fazarah gifted to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, a she-camel from the camels they had acquired at al-Ghabah. He compensated him for it with some compensation, but he was dissatisfied with it. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, upon this pulpit, say: ""A man from the Arabs gives a gift, so I compensate him for it according to what I have, then he is dissatisfied and remains dissatisfied with me. By Allah! After this stance of mine, I will not accept a gift from any Arab man, except from a Qurashi, or an Ansari, or a Thaqafi, or a Dawsi."
"3414","On the authority of Abdullah ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ proposed to a woman from a people called Sawdah. She was a woman with children from a previous marriage (musbiyah), having five or six children from a husband of hers who had died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: ""What prevents you from me?"" She said: ""By Allah, O Prophet of Allah! Nothing prevents me from you except that you are not the most beloved of creation to me, but I honor you lest these children press against your head morning and evening."" He said: ""Is there anything other than that preventing you from me?"" She said: ""No, by Allah!"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: ""May Allah have mercy on you. Indeed, the best women who rode camel saddles are the righteous women of Quraysh: the most compassionate toward a child in infancy, and the most attentive to a husband with what she possesses."""
"3415","On the authority of ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Satirize the Quraysh, for it is more severe upon them than a volley of arrows."" So he sent for Ibn Rawāḥah and said: ""Satirize them."" He satirized them, but it did not please him. Then he sent for Kaʿb ibn Mālik, then he sent for Ḥassān ibn Thābit. When he entered upon him, Ḥassān said: ""It is time for you to send for this lion who strikes with his tail."" Then he stuck out his tongue and began moving it, saying: ""By Him Who sent you with the truth, I shall strip them with my tongue as leather is stripped."" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Do not hasten, for Abū Bakr knows the Quraysh better than anyone regarding their lineages, and I have lineage among them; let him clarify my lineage for you."" So Ḥassān went to him, then returned and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! He has clarified your lineage for me, and by Him Who sent you with the truth, I shall extract you from them as a hair is extracted from dough."" ʿĀʾishah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying to Ḥassān: ""The Holy Spirit will not cease to support you as long as you defend Allah and His Messenger."" And she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: ""Ḥassān satirized them, so he healed and was healed.""Ḥassān said:You satirized Muḥammad, so I answered on his behalf,And with Allah, in that, is the reward.You satirized Muḥammad, a righteous, upright man,The Messenger of Allah, whose character is fidelity.For my father and his father and my honorAre a protection for the honor of Muḥammad from you.May I lose my little daughter if you do not see herStirring up dust from the sides of Kadāʾ,Our mares crossing the reins, ascending,Upon their shoulders are the thirsty, polished spears.Our steeds remain rain-drenched,While women strike them with their veils.If you turn away from us, we shall perform ʿUmrah,And victory shall come and the cover shall be removed.But if not, then be patient for the striking of a dayIn which Allah honors whom He wills.And Allah said: ""I have sent a servantWho speaks the truth, there is no ambiguity in him.""And Allah said: ""I have facilitated a host—They are the Anṣār, their nature is encounter.""For us, on every day from Maʿadd,Is reviling or fighting or satire.So whoever among you satirizes the Messenger of Allah,And praises him and supports him—it is all the same.And Jibrīl is the Messenger of Allah among us,And the Holy Spirit—there is no equal for him."
"3416","[AI-translation] Narrated from Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abd Allah (ibn Zubayr), from his father, from his grandfather, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say at the killing of Hanzalah ibn Abi Amir after he and Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith met, when Shaddad ibn al-Aswad overcame him with the sword and killed him. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""Your companion is being washed by the angels."" They asked his wife, and she said: ""He went out when he heard the tumult while he was in a state of major ritual impurity."" The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""For that reason the angels washed him."
"3417","[AI-translation] He said, peace be upon him and his family: ""Indeed, the scholars, when they meet their Lord, Mighty and Majestic, Mu'adh will be a stone's throw ahead of them."
"3418","[AI-translation] The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""The superiority of Aishah over women is like the superiority of tharid over the rest of the food."" . . It was reported from the hadith of..."
"3419","On the authority of Zayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Saʿīd ibn ʿAmr ibn Nufayl of Banū ʿAdī, from his father, who said: I came to Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Anṣārī accompanied by a group of young men from Quraysh. We entered upon him after his eyesight had failed. We found a rope hanging from the ceiling and loaves of bread placed before him. Whenever a poor person asked for food, Jābir would stand up, take a loaf, hold the rope until he reached the poor person to give it to him, then return by the rope until he sat down. I said to him: ""May Allah grant you well-being. We, when a poor person comes, we give [to him]."" He said: ""I anticipate reward for the walking in this."" Then he said: ""Shall I not inform you of something I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"" They said: ""Yes."" He said: ""I heard him say: 'Indeed, Quraysh are people of trustworthiness; no one seeks to undermine them with stumbling blocks except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will throw him down on his nose.'"""
"3420","'Amr ibn Salamah al-Hamdani said: We used to sit at the door of 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud before the Fajr prayer. When he came out, we would walk with him to the mosque. Abu Musa al-Ash'ari came to us and said: ""Has Abu 'Abd al-Rahman come out to you yet?"" We said: ""No."" So he sat with us until he came out. When he came out, we all stood up to him. Abu Musa said to him: ""O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman! I saw something in the mosque just now that I disapproved of, and I saw nothing, praise be to Allah, but good."" He said: ""What is it?"" He said: ""If you live, you will see it."" He said: ""I saw in the mosque people sitting in circles waiting for the prayer. In each circle there was a man, and in their hands were pebbles. He would say: 'Say Allahu Akbar one hundred times,' and they would say Allahu Akbar one hundred times. Then he would say: 'Say La ilaha illa Allah one hundred times,' and they would say La ilaha illa Allah one hundred times. And he would say: 'Say Subhan Allah one hundred times,' and they would say Subhan Allah one hundred times."" He said: ""What did you say to them?"" He said: ""I did not say anything to them, waiting for your opinion."" He said: ""Why did you not order them to count their evil deeds and guarantee them that nothing of their good deeds would be lost?"" Then he went on, and we went with him until he came to one of those circles. He stood over them and said: ""What is this that I see you doing?"" They said: ""O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman! These are pebbles with which we count the takbir, tahlil, and tasbih."" He said: ""Count your evil deeds, for I guarantee that nothing of your good deeds will be lost. Woe to you, O Ummah of Muhammad! How quickly you go to ruin! These are the Companions of your Prophet ﷺ still abundant, and these are his garments not yet worn out, and his vessels not yet broken. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! You are either on a religion better guided than the religion of Muhammad, or you are opening a door of misguidance."" They said: ""By Allah! O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman! We intended nothing but good."" He said: ""And how many are those who intend good but do not achieve it. Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told us: 'A people will recite the Qur'an, but it will not go beyond their throats. They will pass through Islam as an arrow passes through the target.' And by Allah! I do not know, perhaps most of them are from you."" Then he turned away from them. 'Amr ibn Salamah said: We saw most of those circles fighting against us on the Day of Nahrawan along with the Khawarij."
"3421","Abdullah ibn Buraydah narrated from his father that a black slave woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) when he returned from one of his military expeditions. She said: ""I had vowed that if Allah returned you safely, I would beat the duff (tambourine) in your presence."" He said: ""If you did so, then do it; and if you did not, then do not do it."" So she beat it. Then Abu Bakr entered while she was beating it, and others entered while she was beating it. Then Umar entered, and she put her duff behind her back while she was veiled. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Satan flees from you, O Umar! I was sitting here and these people entered, but when you entered, she did what she did."""
"3422","[AI-translation] Narrated from Jubayr ibn Mut'im who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""A Qurashi has twice the strength of a man not from Quraysh."" It was said to al-Zuhri: ""Why is that?"" He said: ""Due to the sharpness of opinion."
"3423","[AI-translation] Narrated from Samurah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Every prophet has a basin, and they boast about which of them has the most attendees, and I hope by Allah that I will be the one with the most attendees."
"3424","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, elevated to the Prophet: ""Indeed, Allah has angels that roam the earth, conveying to me the salutations of my Ummah."
"3425","Ibn Abbas said: The leaders of Quraysh gathered in the Hijr and made a pact by Al-Lat, Al-Uzza, Manat the third, the other, and Naila and Isaf: ""If we see Muhammad, we will surely rise against him as one man and not leave him until we kill him."" Then his daughter Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) came weeping until she entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and said: ""These leaders of Quraysh have made a pact against you; if they see you, they will surely rise against you and kill you. There is not a man among them except that he has known his share of your blood."" He said: ""O my daughter! Bring me water for ablution."" So he performed ablution, then entered the mosque upon them. When they saw him, they said: ""Here he is."" And they lowered their gazes, their chins fell upon their chests, and they were rooted in their seats. None of them raised their gaze to him, and no man among them rose against him. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) approached until he stood over their heads, took a handful of dust, and said: ""May the faces be humiliated."" Then he threw it at them. No man among them was struck by a pebble from that dust except he was killed on the day of Badr as a disbeliever."
"3426","[AI-translation] Narrated from Umm Salamah who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf entered upon her and said: ""O mother! I fear that the abundance of my wealth will destroy me; I am the wealthiest of Quraysh."" She said: ""O my son! So spend, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: 'Indeed, among my companions are those who will not see me after I part from them.'"" He went out and met Umar, so Umar came and entered upon her and said: ""By Allah! Am I among them?"" She said: ""No, and I will not inform anyone after you."
"3427","[AI-translation] Rahman ibn al-Hadrami who said: One who heard the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, informed me, saying: ""Indeed, there are a people from my Ummah who will be given rewards like those of the first ones; they will forbid evil."
"3428","[AI-translation] Narrated from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Among trees there is a tree whose leaves do not fall, and it is the likeness of the Muslim. So tell me, what is it?"" The people fell to discussing the trees of the valleys. Abd Allah said: ""It occurred to me that it is the date palm, but I felt shy."" Then they said: ""Tell us what it is, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""It is the date palm."
"3429","[AI-translation] Khudri who said: We were sitting waiting for the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, and he came out to us from one of the houses of his wives. He said: We stood up with him, and his sandal broke, so Ali stayed behind to repair it. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, went on, and we went on with him. Then he stood waiting for him, and we stood with him. He said: ""Among you is one who will fight for the interpretation of this Quran just as I fought for its revelation."" We looked expectantly, and among us were Abu Bakr and Umar, but he said: ""No, rather it is the repairer of the sandal."" He said: We went to give him the glad tidings, and it was as if he had already heard it."
"3430","[AI-translation] Tufayl who said: I set off, I and 'Amr ibn Sulay', until we came to Hudhayfah. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, say: ""This tribe of Mudar will not leave for Allah a righteous servant on the earth except that it will afflict him and destroy him, until Allah overtakes them with armies from His servants, humbling them so that they cannot protect the tail of a watercourse."
"3431","[AI-translation] From Siyabah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said on the Day of Hunayn: ""I am the son of al-Awatik."
"3432","On the authority of ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār, from a man of the Anṣār, that Anas al-Anṣārī informed ʿAṭāʾ that he kissed his wife during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) while he was fasting. So he ordered his wife to ask the Prophet (peace be upon him) about that. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Indeed the Messenger of Allah does that."" His wife informed him, so he said: ""Indeed the Prophet (peace be upon him) has concessions in some matters. Go back to him and say to him."" She returned to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and said: ""He says: Indeed the Prophet (peace be upon him) has concessions in some matters."" He said: ""I am the most God-fearing of you for Allah and the most knowledgeable of you regarding the limits of Allah."""
"3433","[AI-translation] From Anas, raised to the Prophet: ""I am the first to take hold of the ring of the door of Paradise, and I will make it rattle."
"3434","[AI-translation] He, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""I am the master of the children of Adam..."" And it is reported from the hadith of........( )"
"3435","[AI-translation] From Anas, raised to the Prophet: ""I am Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah. I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger. I do not like that you elevate me above the station that Allah has placed me in."
"3436","[AI-translation] From Safinah who said: We were (with the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him) on a journey. He said: So whenever a man grew tired, he would throw his clothes upon me, a shield or a sword, until I carried a great deal of that. He said: So the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""You are Safinah."" ( )"
"3437","[AI-translation] From 'A'ishah, that Abu Bakr entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, and said: ""You are the freed one of Allah from the Fire."
"3438","[AI-translation] From 'Amir ibn Shahr who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, say: ""Look at the Quraysh, and take from (in a narration: and listen to) their words, and leave their actions."
"3439","On the authority of Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith, she said: While I was passing by, the Prophet ﷺ was in the Hijr. He said: ""O Umm al-Fadl!"" I replied: ""At your service, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""You are pregnant with a male child."" She said: ""How can that be, when Quraysh have sworn an oath not to give birth to females?"" He said: ""It is as I say to you. When you deliver him, bring him to me."" When she gave birth, she brought him to the Prophet ﷺ. He named him Abdullah, and performed tahneek for him with his saliva. Then he said: ""Take him, for you will find him to be sagacious."" She said: ""I went to al-Abbas and informed him. He dressed up and came to the Prophet ﷺ. He was a handsome man, tall in stature. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him, he stood up for him, kissed him between the eyes, and seated him on his right. Then he said: 'This is my uncle. Whoever wishes may boast of his uncle.' Al-Abbas said: 'Some of the speech, O Messenger of Allah!' He replied: 'Why should I not say it, when you are my uncle and the remnant of my forefathers, and the uncle is like a father.'"""
"3440","[AI-translation] From Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, raised to the Prophet: ""I am only a conveyor, and Allah guides; and a distributor, and Allah gives. So whoever receives from me something with good desire and good guidance, then that is the one who is blessed in it. And whoever receives from me something with bad desire and bad guidance, then that is the one who eats and is not satisfied."
"3441","[AI-translation] From Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah, that a Bedouin pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, to Islam. But the Bedouin was afflicted by a fever in Madinah, so he came to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Relieve me of my pledge."" But the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, refused. Then he came to him and said: ""Relieve me of my pledge,"" and he refused. Then he came to him and said: ""Relieve me of my pledge,"" and he refused. So the Bedouin left, and the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Madinah is like a bellows; it expels its impurity and clarifies its good."
"3442","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas: That Ukaydir Dumat sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) a cloak of silk brocade. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) wore it, and the people marveled at it. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Do you marvel at this? By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, the handkerchiefs of Sa'd bin Mu'adh in Paradise are better than this."" He then gifted it to 'Umar, who said, ""O Messenger of Allah! You dislike it, yet I wear it?"" He said, ""O 'Umar! I only sent it to you so you could send it as a gift, thereby obtaining some wealth."" This was before silk was prohibited."
"3443","On the authority of Amr ibn Abasah: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Who has followed you in this matter?"" He said: ""A free man and a slave."" I said: ""What is Islam?"" He said: ""Good speech and feeding food."" I said: ""What is faith (Iman)?"" He said: ""Patience and generosity."" I said: ""Which Islam is best?"" He said: ""He from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe."" I said: ""Which faith is best?"" He said: ""Good character."" I said: ""Which prayer is best?"" He said: ""Length of standing (in prayer)."" I said: ""Which migration is best?"" He said: ""That you abandon what your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, dislikes."" I said: ""Then which jihad is best?"" He said: ""He whose mount is hamstrung and his blood is shed."" I said: ""Which hour is best?"" He said: ""The middle of the last part of the night..."""
"3444","[AI-translation] He (peace be upon him) said: ""Stay firm, O Hira', for there is none upon you except a Prophet, a Siddiq (truthful one), or a martyr."" It is reported in the hadith of......"
"3445","Sa'id ibn al-'As reported that Aisha, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ (Muslim and others added: ""and Uthman""), narrated to him that Abu Bakr sought permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was reclining on his bed wearing Aisha's mantle. So he permitted Abu Bakr while he was in that state, and he fulfilled his need with him, then he left. Then Umar sought permission, so he permitted him while he was in that same state, and he fulfilled his need with him, then he left. Uthman said: ""Then I sought permission to enter upon him, so he sat up and said to Aisha: 'Gather your clothes upon yourself.' So I fulfilled my need with him, then I left."" Aisha said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Why did I not see you startled for Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, as you were startled for Uthman?"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Indeed, Uthman is a man of modesty, and I feared that if I permitted him in that state, he would not convey his need to me."""
"3446","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir bin Samura, who said: 'Umar bin Al-Khattab delivered a sermon to us at Al-Jabiya and said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) stood among us in the same position as I stand among you today, and said: 'Honor my Companions, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then lying will become widespread, to the extent that a man will testify without being asked to, and will swear without being asked to.'"
"3447","On the authority of Ibn ʿAbbās, he said: I heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb say: When ʿAbdullāh ibn Ubayy died, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was invited to pray over him. He stood up to do so. When he stood over him intending to pray, I moved until I stood at his chest and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! [Will you pray] over the enemy of Allah, ʿAbdullāh ibn Ubayy, who said on such-and-such day such-and-such?"" — enumerating his days. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) kept smiling until I spoke excessively. He said: ""Leave me alone, O ʿUmar. I have been given the choice and I chose. It was said to me: [Quran 9:80] 'Whether you ask forgiveness for them or do not ask forgiveness for them — even if you ask forgiveness for them seventy times, Allah will never forgive them.' If I knew that if I increased beyond seventy he would be forgiven, I would have increased."" Then he prayed over him and walked with him, and stood at his grave until he was finished. He said: I was amazed at myself and my boldness toward the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), but Allah and His Messenger know best. By Allah, it was only a short time until these two verses were revealed: [Quran 9:84] ""And do not pray over any of them who has died ever, nor stand at his grave. Indeed, they disbelieved in Allah and His Messenger and died while they were defiantly disobedient."" Until the end of the verse. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) never prayed over a hypocrite after him, nor stood at his grave, until Allah took him."
"3448","[AI-translation] Hakam bin Abi Al-'As were leaping onto my pulpit like monkeys leap."" It is reported in the hadith of Abu Hurairah, Thauban, and the mursal of Sa'id bin Al-Musayyab, and the wording of the hadith of Abu Hurairah is that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said... then he mentioned it. He said: ""The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) was never seen laughing fully until he passed away."
"3449","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: It was said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Pray against the polytheists."" He said: ""I was not sent as a curser, but I was sent as a mercy."" ( )"
"3450","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: They said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Do you jest with us?"" He said: ""I say nothing but the truth."
"3451","[AI-translation] Khudri, Marfu'an: The Throne shook at the death of Sa'd bin Mu'adh out of the joy of the Lord, Mighty and Majestic. ( )"
"3452","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family), while the funeral bier of Sa'd was placed, said: ""The Throne of the Most Merciful shook for him."" The hypocrites in his funeral began to say, ""How light it is!"" This reached the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family), so he said: ""It was only that the angels were carrying him along with them."" ( )"
"3453","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Uqba bin 'Amir, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: ""The people of Yemen have the most tender hearts, the softest innermost hearts, and are the most responsive in obedience."
"3454","[AI-translation] Zubair bin Al-'Awwam, who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) was wearing two coats of armor on the day of Uhud. He tried to climb up to the rock but could not, so Talha sat beneath him, and the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) climbed onto him until he was upright on the rock. He said: I heard the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) say: ""Talha has made Paradise obligatory."" ( )"
"3455","[AI-translation] From Aishah, elevated: ""Verily, the first of people to perish will be your people, and the first of Quraysh to perish will be the people of my household."
"3456","[AI-translation] From Aishah, she said: Two men entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, and spoke to him about something—I do not know what it was—and they angered him, so he cursed them and reviled them. When they left, I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Who attained any good such as these two attained?"" He said: ""And what is that?"" She said: I said: ""You cursed them and reviled them."" He said: ""Did you not know what I stipulated with my Lord? I said: 'O Allah, I am but a human; so whichever Muslim I curse or revile, make it for him purification and reward.'"
"3457","From Abu Fakhita, who said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited us and stayed overnight with us, and Al-Hasan and Al-Husayn were sleeping. Al-Hasan asked for water, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up to a water skin of ours and squeezed it into a cup, then gave him to drink. Al-Husayn reached out to drink, but he prevented him and started with Al-Hasan. Fatima said: O Messenger of Allah! It seems as if he is more beloved to you. He said: No, but he asked for water first. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Indeed, I and you, and these two, and this sleeping one — meaning Ali — will be in one place on the Day of Resurrection. That is, Fatima and her two sons: Al-Hasan and Al-Husayn."
"3458","Amr ibn Abi Qurra said: Hudhayfah was in al-Mada'in, and he would narrate things that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to some of his companions in anger. People who heard this from Hudhayfah would go to Salman and tell him Hudhayfah's statement. Salman would say: ""Hudhayfah knows best what he says."" They would return to Hudhayfah and say: ""We mentioned your statement to Salman, and he neither confirmed you nor denied you."" So Hudhayfah came to Salman while he was in a date-drying place (mabqala) and said: ""O Salman! What prevents you from confirming me regarding what I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"" Salman said: ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would become angry and say things in his anger to some of his companions, and he would become pleased and say things in his pleasure to some of his companions. Will you not stop until you make men love men and hate men, and until you cause disagreement and division? And you certainly know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon and said: 'Any man of my nation whom I insulted with an insult or cursed with a curse in my anger - for I am only a son of Adam, I get angry as they get angry, and I was only sent as a mercy to the worlds - so make it a prayer for them on the Day of Resurrection.' By Allah, you will certainly stop, or I will write to Umar."""
"3459","Muhammad ibn Sa'd narrated from his father who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab sought permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and with him were women from Quraysh asking him and requesting more from him, their voices raised above his voice. When Umar sought permission, they hurried to the hijab. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) gave him permission, so he entered while the Prophet (peace be upon him) was laughing. He said: ""May Allah keep your teeth laughing, O Messenger of Allah! May my father and mother be sacrificed for you."" He said: ""I am amazed at these women who were with me; when they heard your voice, they hurried to the hijab."" He said: ""You are more deserving that they fear you, O Messenger of Allah."" Then he turned to them and said: ""O enemies of yourselves! You fear me but you do not fear the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)?"" They said: ""You are harsher and sterner than the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)."" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Ah, O son of al-Khattab! By Him in Whose Hand is my soul! The devil never meets you traveling a path but he takes a path other than yours."""
"3460","[AI-translation] Khudri, he said: The people complained about Ali—may Allah be pleased with him—so the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, stood among us as a preacher, and I heard him saying: ""O people! Do not complain about Ali, for by Allah! He is better in the cause of Allah, or in the path of Allah, than to be complained about."
"3461","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas, elevated: The four sisters: Maymunah, Umm al-Fadl, Salma, and Asma bint Umays—their maternal sister—are believers."
"3462","[AI-translation] From Sahl bin Sa'd that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""The Ansar are the inner garment and the people are the outer garment. And if the people were to face a valley or a mountain pass, and the Ansar were to face a valley, I would traverse the valley of the Ansar. And were it not for the Hijrah, I would be a man from the Ansar."
"3463","[AI-translation] The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""The Ansar are my inner garment and my intimate ones. And the people will increase and decrease, so accept from their good-doers and overlook their evil-doers."" It came from the hadith... ( )"
"3464","[AI-translation] Bara' bin 'Azib, may Allah be pleased with him, elevated: ""The Ansar are not loved except by a believer, and are not hated except by a hypocrite. So whoever loves them, Allah loves him, and whoever hates them, Allah hates him."
"3465","[AI-translation] The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Give glad tidings to Khadijah of a house in Paradise of hollow pearls, in which there is no clamor and no toil."" It came from the hadith......"
"3466","On the authority of Abū Umāmah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to my people, (the tribe of) Bahilah. (I reached them while I was hungry.) I came upon them while they were eating food, (and in another narration: they were eating blood). They brought me back with them and honored me. They said: ""Welcome, O al-Ṣudayy ibn ʿAjlān!"" They said: ""We have heard that you have apostatized to this man."" I said: ""No, but I have believed in Allah and His Messenger, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to you to present to you Islam and its laws."" They said: ""Come, eat."" I said: ""(Woe to you! Verily) I have only come to forbid you from this, and I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; I have come to you that you may believe in him."" (So I began calling them to Islam.) They denied me and reviled me. I said to them: ""Woe to you! Bring me some water, for I am severely thirsty."" He said: ""And I had my turban on me."" They said: ""No, but we will leave you to die of thirst."" So I departed, hungry and thirsty, with severe exhaustion having befallen me. He said: So I wrapped my turban, laid my head in the turban, and slept on the hot sand in intense heat. Then in my sleep I was brought a draught of milk, the like of which people have never seen more delicious. He enabled me to drink it, so I drank, was satiated, and my belly swelled. The people said: ""A man from the best and noblest of you came to you, and you rejected him. Go to him and feed him whatever food and drink he desires."" They brought me food. I said: ""I have no need for your food or drink, for Allah has fed me and given me drink."" They looked at the state I was in. I showed them my belly, they looked, and they believed in me and in what I brought from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, (and they all embraced Islam)."
"3467","On the authority of ʿAbdullāh ibn Najiyy, from his father, who said: I traveled with ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), and I was the carrier of his water vessel. When we passed by Nineveh while he was on his way to Ṣiffīn, ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) called out: ""Be patient, Abū ʿAbdullāh! Be patient, Abū ʿAbdullāh, by the bank of the Euphrates!"" I said: ""And what is that?"" He said: ""I entered upon the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) one day, and his eyes were overflowing with tears. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, has someone angered you? Why are your eyes overflowing?' He said: 'Rather, Gabriel came to me just now and informed me that al-Ḥusayn will be killed by the bank of the Euphrates.' He said: 'Would you like me to let you smell his soil?' I said: 'Yes.' So he extended his hand, took a handful of dust, and gave it to me, and I could not prevent my eyes from overflowing."""
"3468","[AI-translation] The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""While I was at a well drawing water from it, Abu Bakr and Umar came to me. Abu Bakr took the bucket and drew one or two bucketfuls, and in his drawing there was some weakness—may Allah forgive him. Then Ibn al-Khattab took it from the hand of Abu Bakr, and it transformed in his hand into a large bucket. I never saw a masterful person among the people perform as he performed, and he drew until the people settled at the watering place."" It came from the hadith... ( )"
"3469","[AI-translation] From Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunayf, from some of the Companions of the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, that the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""While I was sleeping, I saw the people being presented to me, wearing shirts, some of which reached the chest and some of which reached lower than that. Then Umar was presented to me, wearing a shirt that he was dragging."" They said: ""What did you interpret it as, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""The religion."
"3470","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, drew four lines in the earth, then said: ""Do you know what this is?"" They said: ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""The best of the women of Paradise are Khadijah bint Khuwaylid, Fatimah bint Muhammad, peace be upon him, Maryam bint 'Imran, and Asiyah bint Muzahim, the wife of Pharaoh."
"3471","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, passed away while a striped woolen garment was being woven for him."
"3472","On the authority of Al-Barā' ibn 'Āzib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was approached, and it was said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Indeed Abū Sufyān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn 'Abd al-Muṭṭalib satirizes you."" So Ibn Rawāḥah stood up and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Permit me to deal with him."" He said: ""Are you the one who says 'Allah has made firm'?"" He said: ""Yes."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah: So may Allah make firm what He gave you of the good firmness of Mūsā and a victory like their victory."" He said: ""And you, may Allah do good to you similarly."" Then Ka'b jumped up and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Permit me to deal with him."" He said: ""Are you the one who says 'She intended'?"" He said: ""Yes."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah: Sakīnah intended to contend with her Lord, so the Contender of contenders will surely overcome."" He said: ""Indeed Allah has not forgotten that for you."" Then Ḥassān stood up and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Permit me to deal with him,"" and he stuck out a black tongue for him. He said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Permit me, if you wish I will pierce the water-skin with it."" He said: ""Go to Abū Bakr so he may inform you of the news of the people and their days and their lineages, then satirize them, and Jibrīl is with you."""
"3473","[AI-translation] From Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: I sat with the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, more than a hundred times. His companions would recite poetry and recall things from the affairs of the pre-Islamic period while he remained silent, and sometimes he would smile with them."
"3474","Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: My father ordered me to prepare a khazīrah, so I prepared it. Then he ordered me to take it to the Prophet ﷺ. I came to him while he was in his house. He said to me: ""What do you have with you, O Jābir, is it meat?"" I said: ""No."" So I went back to my father, and he said to me: ""Did you see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"" I said: ""Yes."" He said: ""Then why did you not hear him say something?"" I said: ""Yes, he said: 'What do you have with you, O Jābir, is it meat?'"" He thought perhaps the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a desire for it, so he ordered a domesticated sheep of ours to be slaughtered, then ordered it to be roasted, then ordered me to take it to the Prophet ﷺ. He said to me: ""What do you have with you, O Jābir?"" I informed him, so he said: ""May Allah reward the Anṣār on our behalf with good, especially ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥarām and Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah."""
"3475","[AI-translation] From Khalid ibn Ma'dan, who said: Al-Miqdam ibn Ma'di Karib and 'Amr ibn al-Aswad went as a delegation to Mu'awiyah. Mu'awiyah said to al-Miqdam: ""Do you know that al-Hasan ibn 'Ali has passed away?"" Al-Miqdam said: ""To Allah we belong and to Him we return."" Mu'awiyah said to him: ""Do you consider it a calamity?"" He replied: ""Why should I not consider it a calamity, when the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, placed him in his lap and said: 'Al-Hasan is from me, and al-Husayn is from 'Ali,' may Allah the Almighty be pleased with them both."
"3476","[AI-translation] He, peace be upon him, said: ""Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the masters of the youth of the people of Paradise."" Transmitted from the hadith of......"
"3477","[AI-translation] Tirmidhi, Book of Merits, Chapter of the Merits of al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them, no. (3701)"
"3478","[AI-translation] From Ibn Shihab that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Hadhramaut is better than Banu al-Harith."
"3479","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Take the Qur'an from four: from Ibn Mas'ud, Ubayy ibn Ka'b, Mu'adh ibn Jabal, and Salim, the mawla of Abu Hudhayfah."
"3480","On the authority of Abu Nadrah, from Abdullah ibn Mawalah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: While I was traveling in Al-Ahwaz, I encountered a man riding ahead of me on a mule or a female mule. He was supplicating: ""O Allah, my generation from this ummah has passed away, so join me with them."" I said: ""And I as well, so include me in your supplication."" He said: ""And this companion of mine, if he wishes that."" Then he said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: 'The best of my ummah is my generation, then those who follow them.'"" He said: ""And I do not know whether he mentioned the third or not."" Then he said: ""Then there will come after them a people among whom obesity will appear; they will give testimony without being asked for it."" He said: ""And behold, it was Buraydah al-Aslami."""
"3481","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: ""The best of my nation is the generation in whom I was sent, then those who follow them, (then those who follow them). And Allah knows best whether he mentioned the third or not. Then there will succeed a people who love plumpness, who testify before they are asked to testify."
"3482","[AI-translation] From 'Imran ibn Husayn, raised to the Prophet: ""The best of my nation is the generation in whom I was sent, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. And Allah knows best whether he mentioned the third or not. Then there will appear a people who testify without being asked to testify, promise without fulfilling, betray and cannot be trusted, and among whom fatness will spread."
"3483","[AI-translation] On the authority of Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, marfu'an: The best of the people of the East is 'Abd al-Qays; mankind embraced Islam unwillingly, while they embraced Islam willingly."
"3484","[AI-translation] On the authority of Usayr bin Jabir: That 'Umar bin al-Khattab said to Uways al-Qarni: ""Seek forgiveness for me."" He said: ""You are more entitled to seek forgiveness for me; you are one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family."" He said: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: 'The best of the Tabi'un is a man from Qarn called Uways.'"
"3485","[AI-translation] Khattab, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, say: ""The best of people is my generation, the one I am among, then those who follow them, [then those who follow them]. Then a people will emerge among whom fatness will spread; they will testify without being asked, and there will be clamor in their markets."
"3486","[AI-translation] On the authority of 'Imran bin Husayn, marfu'an: ""The best of people is my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then a people will come who grow fat, loving fatness; they will utter the testimony before being asked for it."
"3487","[AI-translation] On the authority of 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, marfu'an: ""The best of people is my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then a people will come whose testimony precedes his oath, and whose oath precedes his testimony."
"3488","[AI-translation] On the authority of Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, marfu'an: ""The best of women who ride camels are the righteous women of Quraysh; they are the most tender towards a child in its childhood, and the most mindful of a husband concerning what is in his possession."
"3489","[AI-translation] On the authority of Abu Hurayrah, marfu'an: ""The best of you is the best of you towards my family after me."
"3490","[AI-translation] Sha'bi, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, likened three men from the clan of Umayyah, and said: ""Dihyah al-Kalbi resembles Jibril, 'Urwah bin Mas'ud al-Thaqafi resembles 'Isa son of Maryam, and 'Abd al-'Uzza resembles the Dajjal."
"3491","[AI-translation] On the authority of 'Abdullah bin Buraydah, from his father, marfu'an: ""I entered Paradise, and a young maiden met me, so I said: 'Whose are you?' She said: 'I am for Zayd bin Harithah, may Allah be pleased with him.'"
"3492","[AI-translation] On the authority of 'Aishah, marfu'an: ""I entered Paradise and heard recitation in it. I said: 'Who is this?' They said: 'Harithah bin al-Nu'man. Such is piety, such is piety.'"" (And he was the most dutiful of people to his mother.)"
"3493","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Umar: Hatim was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family), and he said: ""That is a man who desired a matter and attained it."
"3494","[AI-translation] Narrated Mujashi' bin Mas'ud: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) with my brother Mujalid after the Conquest, and I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, I have brought you my brother Mujalid so you may pledge allegiance to him for emigration."" He said: ""The people of emigration have taken what is in it."" I said: ""Then upon what do you pledge allegiance to him, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""I pledge allegiance to him upon Islam, faith, and Jihad."
"3495","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Amr bin Hurayth: My mother took me to the Prophet (peace be upon him) while I was a young boy, so he wiped over my head and supplicated for provision for me. (In a narration: for blessing)."
"3496","[AI-translation] Bahili: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""My mother saw as if a light emerged from her, by which the palaces of Sham were illuminated."
"3497","[AI-translation] He (peace be upon him) said: ""I saw Ja'far bin Abi Talib as an angel flying in Paradise with the angels, having two wings."" (Narration from a hadith...)"
"3498","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Umar: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""I saw many black sheep into which many white sheep entered."" They said: ""What did you interpret it as, O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family)?"" He said: ""The non-Arabs will share in your religion and your lineages."" They said: ""The non-Arabs, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""If faith were suspended in the Pleiades, men from the non-Arabs would attain it, and they are the happiest of people with it."
"3499","On the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""I saw in a dream as if I were in a secure coat of armor, and I saw cows slaughtered. So I interpreted the secure coat of armor as Medina, and the cows — by Allah! — as good (martyrdom)."" He said: So he said to his companions: ""If we stay in Medina, then if they enter upon us therein, we will fight them."" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah! By Allah! We were not entered upon therein during the pre-Islamic period, so how would we be entered upon therein in Islam?"" 'Affan said in his narration: So he said: ""Your affair then."" He said: So he put on his armor. He said: So the Ansar said: ""We have returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) his opinion."" So they came and said: ""O Prophet of Allah! Your affair then."" He said: ""It is not for a prophet, when he has put on his armor, to take it off until he fights."""
"3500","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: I saw myself entering Paradise, and there I was with Ar-Rumaysa', the wife of Abu Talhah. And I heard a sound in front of me, so I said: ""Who is this, O Jibril?"" He said: ""This is Bilal."" And I saw a white palace, in its courtyard was a maiden. I said: ""Whose is this palace?"" He said: ""For 'Umar bin Al-Khattab."" I wanted to enter and look at it, but I remembered your protective jealousy. 'Umar said: ""May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah! Would I be jealous over you?"
"3501","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Abdullah: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""I am pleased for my Ummah with what Ibn Umm 'Abd is pleased for it."
"3502","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""Zainab is the best (in a narration: the most superior) of my daughters who was afflicted through me."" This reached 'Ali bin Husain, so he came to him and said: ""What is this hadith reaching me from you, in which you belittle Fatimah?"" 'Urwah said: ""I would not love to have such and such, and that I belittle Fatimah of a right that is hers. And after that, it is upon me that I will never narrate it again."
"3503","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Az-Zubair is the son of my maternal aunt, and my disciple from my Ummah."
"3504","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, raised to the Prophet (ﷺ): ""I asked Allah, Mighty and Majestic, for intercession for my Ummah, and He said to me: 'For you are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without account.' I said: 'O Lord! Increase for me.' He said: 'Then for you is thus,' and He scooped with His hands in front of Him, and to His right, and to His left."
"3505","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas, may Allah the Almighty be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""I asked my Lord a question which I wished I had not asked. I said: 'O Lord! There were messengers before me; among them were those whom You subjugated the winds for, and among them were those who used to bring the dead to life, (and You spoke to Musa).' He said: 'Did I not find you an orphan and give you shelter? Did I not find you astray and guide you? Did I not find you in need and make you self-sufficient? Did I not expand your breast for you, and remove from you your burden?' He said: 'I said: Yes, O Lord! (And I wished I had not asked Him).'"
"3506","[AI-translation] From Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: ""The master of the martyrs is Hamzah bin 'Abd al-Muttalib, and a man who stood up to an unjust imam, commanding him and forbidding him, so he killed him."
"3507","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas, raised to the Prophet (ﷺ): ""The best of the women of Paradise after Maryam bint 'Imran are Fatimah, Khadijah, and Asiyah, the wife of Fir'awn."
"3508","[AI-translation] Rahman bin 'Awf, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""I witnessed the pact of al-Mutayyabin with my uncles while I was a young boy, and I would not love to have red camels if I were to break it."
"3509","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah who said: ""I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) supplicating for this clan of (al-Nakha')—or he said: praising them—until I wished I were a man from among them."
"3510","[AI-translation] From Abu Umamah, raised to the Prophet (ﷺ): ""The choicest part of Allah's earth is al-Sham, and in it is the choicest of His creation and His servants. And a group from my Ummah shall enter Paradise, with no account upon them and no punishment."
"3511","[AI-translation] From Zaid bin Thabit, raised to the Prophet (ﷺ): ""Tuba for al-Sham, for the angels of the Most Merciful spread their wings over it."
"3512","[AI-translation] From Abu Umamah who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Tuba for the one who saw me and believed in me, and Tuba seven times for the one who did not see me and believed in me."
"3513","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah bin Busr, a companion of the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Tuba for the one who saw me, and Tuba for the one who saw the one who saw me, and for the one who saw the one who saw the one who saw me and believed in me."
"3514","[AI-translation] Batin who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Aishah is my wife in Paradise."
"3515","[AI-translation] From Jabir ibn Abdullah, marfu': ""Uthman is in Paradise."
"3516","[AI-translation] From Thawban, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him and his family, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, who said: ""Two groups from my Ummah, Allah has secured them from the Fire: a group that invades India, and a group that will be with Isa ibn Maryam, peace be upon them both."
"3517","[AI-translation] He said, peace be upon him and his family: ""'Ali will pay my debt."" Narrated from the hadith of......."
"3518","[AI-translation] From Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: ""'Amr ibn al-'As is among the righteous of Quraysh."
"3519","[AI-translation] He said, peace be upon him: ""Al-Abbas is the uncle of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, and indeed the uncle of a man is the counterpart of his father."
"3520","[AI-translation] From Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Harshness of hearts and coarseness are in the East, and faith is among the people of the Hijaz."
"3521","[AI-translation] Miswar, that he sent Hasan ibn Hasan to him to propose to his daughter. He said to him: ""Tell him to meet me at nightfall."" He said: So he met him, and al-Miswar praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: ""As for what follows! By Allah, there is no lineage, nor tie, nor marriage relationship more beloved to me than your lineage (and your tie) and your marriage relationship. But the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: 'Fatimah is a part of me; what distresses her distresses me, and what pleases her pleases me. And lineages on the Day of Resurrection will be severed except my lineage, my tie, and my marriage relationship.' And you have her daughter with you, and if I were to marry her to you, that would distress her. So he left, having an excuse for him."
"3522","[AI-translation] From Umm Hani, marfu': Allah favored Quraysh with seven traits: 1- He favored them in that they worshipped Allah for ten years, with none but a Qurashi worshipping Him. 2- And He favored them in that He granted them victory on the Day of the Elephant while they were polytheists. 3- And He favored them in that a surah from the Qur'an was revealed concerning them, in which no one else besides them was included: ""For the accustomed security of the Quraysh"" (Quraysh). 4- And He favored them in that among them is prophethood. 5- And the caliphate. 6- And the custodianship. 7- And the providing of water."
"3523","[AI-translation] From Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: ""In every generation of my Ummah are forerunners. ( )"
"3524","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah bin 'Amr, elevated [to the Prophet]: The killer of 'Ammar and his despoiler are in the Fire."
"3525","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik, who said: When the people of Yemen came, the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""The people of Yemen have arrived, and they are softer of heart than you."" (Anas said): And they were the first to introduce handshaking."
"3526","[AI-translation] From Iyas bin Salama, my father narrated to me, saying: We arrived at Al-Hudaybiyah with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and we were fourteen hundred, and it had fifty sheep that did not water it. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) sat at the edge of the well, and either he supplicated or spat into it. He said: So it gushed forth, and we watered and drew water. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) called us for the pledge under the tree. He said: So I pledged to him first among the people, then he pledged, and he pledged until he was in the middle of the people. He said: ""Pledge, O Salamah!"" He said: I said: ""I have already pledged to you, O Messenger of Allah, among the first of the people!"" He said: ""And again."" He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) saw me unarmed, meaning I had no weapon. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) gave me a shield or a buckler, then he pledged until he was at the end of the people. He said: ""Will you not pledge to me, O Salamah?"" He said: I said: ""I have already pledged to you, O Messenger of Allah, among the first of the people and in the middle of the people."" He said: ""And again."" He said: So I pledged to him a third time. Then he said to me: ""O Salamah, where is your shield or buckler that I gave you?"" He said: I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, my uncle 'Amir met me unarmed, so I gave it to him."" He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) laughed and said: ""You are like the one who said the first time: 'O Allah, bring me a beloved who is dearer to me than myself.'"" He said: Then the polytheists sent us a message for a truce until some of us walked among others, and we made peace. He said: And I was a client of Talha bin 'Ubaidullah; I watered his horse, groomed it, and served him, and I ate from his food, and I had left my family and wealth as an emigrant to Allah and His Messenger (peace be upon him). He said: When we made peace with the people of Mecca and mingled with each other, I came to a tree, cleared its thorns, and lay down at its base. He said: Four polytheists from the people of Mecca came to me and began speaking ill of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). I hated them, so I moved to another tree, and they hung their weapons and lay down. While they were like that, a caller called from the bottom of the valley: ""O Emigrants! Ibn Zunaim has been killed!"" He said: I drew my sword and attacked those four while they were sleeping. I took their weapons and gathered them in my hand. He said: Then I said: ""By the One who honored the face of Muhammad (peace be upon him)! Let none of you raise his head, or I will strike the one with eyes."" He said: Then I brought them, driving them to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). He said: And my uncle 'Amir brought a man from the 'Abalat named Mikraz, leading him to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) on a saddled horse, among seventy polytheists. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) looked at them and said: ""Leave them, let them be the beginning of wickedness and its second."" So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) pardoned them, and Allah revealed: ""And He it is Who restrained their hands from you and your hands from them in the valley of Makkah after He had given you victory over them."" [Al-Fath: 24] The whole verse. He said: Then we set out returning to Medina and stopped at a place where there was a mountain between us and Banu Lahyan, who were polytheists. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) sought forgiveness for whoever ascended this mountain that night as if he were a scout for the Prophet (peace be upon him) and his companions. Salamah said: So I climbed that night twice or thrice. Then we arrived in Medina, and the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) sent his riding animals with Rabah, the servant of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and I was with him. I went out with him with the horse of Talha, which I was to send to graze with the animals. When morning came, 'Abdul-Rahman Al-Fazari had made a raid on the riding animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), drove them all away, and killed their shepherd. He said: So I said: ""O Rabah, take this horse and deliver it to Talha bin 'Ubaidullah, and inform the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) that the polytheists have raided his animals."" He said: Then I stood on a hill, faced Medina, and called out three times: ""O morning!"" Then I went out in the tracks of the people, shooting arrows at them and reciting rajaz:
I am the son of Al-Akwa', and today is the day of suckling.
He said: I caught up with one of them and shot an arrow into his mount until the arrowhead pierced his shoulder. He said: I said:
Take it! And I am the son of Al-Akwa', and today is the day of suckling.
He said: By Allah, I did not stop shooting them and hampering their mounts. Whenever a horseman turned to me, I went to a tree and sat at its base, then shot him and hampered his mount until they entered a narrow pass in the mountain. I climbed the mountain and began pelting them with stones. He said: I continued doing that, pursuing them, until every camel from the riding animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) that Allah created, I left behind me, and they left me alone with it. Then I followed them, shooting them until they discarded more than thirty cloaks and thirty spears to lighten their load. They did not throw anything except that I placed a marker of stones on it, which the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and his companions would recognize. Until they came to a narrow pass of a mountain, Fulan bin Badr Al-Fazari came to them. They sat down to eat lunch, and I sat at the edge of a peak. Al-Fazari said: ""What is this I see?"" They said: ""We have met from this one a fierce battle. By Allah, he has not left us since dawn, shooting at us until he snatched everything in our hands."" He said: ""Let a group of four of you stand up against him."" He said: So four of them climbed the mountain towards me. He said: When they were within speaking distance, I said: ""Do you know me?"" They said: ""No, who are you?"" He said: I said: ""I am Salamah bin Al-Akwa'. By the One who honored the face of Muhammad (peace be upon him), I will pursue any one of you and catch him, and none of you will pursue me and catch me."" One of them said: ""I think so."" He said: So they retreated. I did not leave my place until I saw the horsemen of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) threading through the trees. He said: The first of them was Al-Akhram Al-Asadi, followed by Abu Qatadah Al-Ansari, and followed by Al-Miqdad bin Al-Aswad Al-Kindi. He said: I took the rein of Al-Akhram. He said: They turned away in retreat. I said: ""O Akhram, beware of them, lest they cut you off until the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and his companions catch up."" He said: ""O Salamah, if you believe in Allah and the Last Day, and know that Paradise is true and the Fire is true, then do not stand between me and martyrdom."" He said: So I let him go. He and 'Abdul-Rahman met. He said: He hamstrung 'Abdul-Rahman's horse, and 'Abdul-Rahman stabbed him and killed him, and transferred to his horse. Abu Qatadah, the horseman of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), caught up with 'Abdul-Rahman and stabbed him, killing him. He said: By the One who honored the face of Muhammad (peace be upon him), I followed them running on my feet until I could not see behind me any of the companions of Muhammad (peace be upon him), nor their dust, until they turned before sunset to a pass with water called Dhu Qarad, to drink from it, and they were thirsty. He said: They saw me running behind them, so I drove them away from it, meaning I made them leave it, and they did not taste a drop from it. He said: And they went out and ran in a pass. He said: I ran and caught up with one of them, and shot him with an arrow in the joint of his shoulder. He said: I said:
Take it! And I am the son of Al-Akwa', and today is the day of suckling.
He said: ""May his mother be bereft of him! Akwa' in the morning?"" He said: I said: ""Yes, O enemy of his own soul, Akwa' in the morning."" He said: And they left two horses at the pass. He said: I brought them, driving them to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). He said: And my uncle 'Amir caught up with me with a skin containing a little milk, and a skin containing water. I performed ablution and drank, then I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) while he was at the water from which I had driven them away. There was the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) having taken those camels and everything I had rescued from the polytheists, and every spear and cloak. And Bilal had slaughtered a camel from the camels I rescued from the people, and he was roasting its liver and hump for the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). He said: I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, let me select a hundred men from the people, so I can pursue them and kill every last one of them."" He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) laughed until his canines appeared in the light of the fire, and said: ""O Salamah, do you think you would have done that?"" I said: ""Yes, by the One who honored you."" He said: ""They are now settling in the land of Ghatafan."" He said: A man from Ghatafan came and said: ""So-and-so slaughtered a camel for them, and when they skinned it, they saw dust, and said: 'The people have come to you,' so they fled."" He said: When morning came, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""The best of our horsemen today is Abu Qatadah, and the best of our footmen is Salamah."" He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) gave me two shares: the share of a horseman and the share of a footman, combining them both for me. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) seated me behind him on Al-'Adba' returning to Medina. He said: While we were traveling, there was a man from the Ansar who could not be overtaken in a run. He said: He kept saying: ""Is there no one to race to Medina? Is there no racer?"" He kept repeating this. He said: When I heard his words, I said: ""Do you not honor a noble one, and fear a chief?"" He said: ""No, unless it is the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)."" He said: I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, by my father and mother, let me race the man."" He said: ""If you wish."" He said: I said: ""Go ahead."" I folded my legs and sprang up and ran. He said: I tied up a hill or two to catch my breath, then ran after him. I tied up a hill or two, then I lifted myself until I caught him. He said: I struck him between his shoulders. He said: I said: ""You have been beaten, by Allah!"" He said: ""I think so."" He said: So I beat him to Medina. He said: By Allah, we only stayed three nights before we went out to Khaybar with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). He said: My uncle 'Amir used to recite rajaz to the people:
By Allah, were it not for Allah, we would not have been guided, nor given charity, nor prayed. And we are never independent of Your grace. So make the feet firm if we meet, and send down tranquility upon us.
The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Who is this?"" He said: ""I am 'Amir."" He said: ""May your Lord forgive you."" He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) never sought forgiveness for a specific person except that he was martyred. He said: 'Umar bin Al-Khattab called out while he was on his camel: ""O Prophet of Allah, did you not let us enjoy 'Amir for longer?"" He said: When we arrived at Khaybar, he said: Their king, Marhab, came out swinging his sword and saying:
Khaybar knows that I am Marhab, a wielder of weapons, a tested warrior. When wars approach, they blaze.
He said: My uncle 'Amir went out to him and said:
Khaybar knows that I am 'Amir, a wielder of weapons, a daring warrior.
He said: They exchanged two blows. The sword of Marhab fell into the shield of 'Amir, and 'Amir went to strike him from below, but his sword rebounded on himself and cut his forearm's vein, and that was the cause of his death. Salamah said: I went out and saw a group of the companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him) saying: ""The deed of 'Amir is void, he killed himself."" He said: I came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) crying and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, is the deed of 'Amir void?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Who said that?"" He said: I said: ""Some of your companions."" He said: ""Whoever said that has lied; rather, he has his reward twice."" Then he sent me to 'Ali, who was suffering from eye inflammation, and said: ""I will give the banner to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, or whom Allah and His Messenger love."" He said: So I went to 'Ali and brought him, leading him while he had eye inflammation, until I brought him to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). He spat in his eyes, and he was cured. He gave him the banner. And Marhab came out and said:
Khaybar knows that I am Marhab, a wielder of weapons, a tested warrior. When wars approach, they blaze.
'Ali said:
I am the one my mother named Haydar, like a lion of the thickets, fierce in appearance. I will repay them with the measure of Sandarah.
He said: He struck the head of Marhab and killed him, and the conquest was at his hands."
"3527","[AI-translation] Hudhayl who said: There were some people from Rabi'ah with 'Amr bin Al-'As, and a man from Bakr bin Wa'il said: ""Quraysh must come to an end, or else Allah will make this affair in a majority of the Arabs other than them."" 'Amr bin Al-'As said: ""You have lied. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: 'Quraysh are the rulers of the people in good and evil until the Day of Resurrection.'"
"3528","Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) passed away while Abu Bakr was among a group in Medina. He said: He came, uncovered his face, kissed him, and said: ""May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, how good you are alive and dead. Muhammad has died, by the Lord of the Ka'bah."" Then he narrated the hadith. He said: Abu Bakr and Umar set out, walking side by side, until they reached them. Abu Bakr spoke and did not leave anything that was revealed concerning the Ansar, nor anything the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) mentioned about their status, except that he mentioned it. And he said: ""You certainly know that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: 'If the people took a valley and the Ansar took a valley, I would take the valley of the Ansar.' And you certainly know, O Sa'd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: 'While you are sitting, Quraysh are the leaders of this matter; the righteousness of the people follows their righteousness, and their wickedness follows their wickedness.'"" He said: Sa'd said to him: ""You have spoken the truth. We are the ministers and you are the commanders."""
"3529","From Salih ibn Jubayr, who said: Abu Jumu'ah al-Ansari, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), came to us at Bayt al-Maqdis to pray therein, and with us was Raja' ibn Haywah on that day. When he finished, we went out with him to see him off. When we wanted to leave, he said: ""You have a right upon me and a duty that I narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)."" We said: ""Tell us, may Allah have mercy on you."" He said: ""We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and with us was Mu'adh ibn Jabal, the tenth of ten. We said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Are there any people greater than us in reward? We believed in you and followed you.' He said: 'What prevents you from that, while the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) is among you, bringing you revelation from heaven? Rather, a people will come after you to whom a book will come between two covers; they will believe in it and act upon what is in it. Those are greater than you in reward.'"""
"3530","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: ""The one who stands after me is in Paradise (and the one who stands after him is in Paradise), and the third and the fourth are in Paradise."
"3531","[AI-translation] From Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: Whenever the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) was brought something, he would say: ""Take this to so-and-so, for she was a friend of Khadijah; take this to so-and-so, for she loved Khadijah."
"3532","[AI-translation] From Bakr bin 'Abdullah who said: The companions of the Prophet used to throw watermelons at each other, but when it came to serious matters, they were the [true] men."
"3533","[AI-translation] From Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: His (peace be upon him and his family) eyes would sleep, but his heart would not sleep."
"3534","[AI-translation] From Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) had large hands and feet, and a handsome face. I have not seen anyone like him before or after him."
"3535","[AI-translation] From 'Aishah, the Mother of the Believers, who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) had his thigh uncovered, and Abu Bakr sought permission to enter, so he gave him permission while he was in that state. Then 'Umar sought permission, and he gave him permission while he was in that state. Then 'Uthman sought permission, and he lowered his garments over himself. When they stood up, I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr sought permission to enter while you were in that state..."" (And in it) He said: ""O 'Aishah, should I not be shy before a man by whom the angels feel shy!"
"3536","[AI-translation] From 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, raised to the Prophet: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, was not such that anyone who saw him would be deluded about him."
"3537","[AI-translation] From Usamah ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace be upon him: That he used to take him and al-Hasan and say: ""O Allah, I love them both, so love them both."
"3538","[AI-translation] Jadali, he said: Umm Salamah said to me: ""Is the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, insulted among you upon the pulpits?"" I said: ""Glory be to Allah! And how could the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, be insulted?"" She said: ""Is not 'Ali ibn Abi Talib insulted, and whoever loves him? I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, used to love him."
"3539","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah: That the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, used to tie a stone on his stomach out of hunger."
"3540","[AI-translation] From Jabir: He, peace be upon him and his family, used to offer himself to the people at the Mawqif and say: ""Is there not a man who will carry me to his people? For Quraysh have prevented me from conveying the words of my Lord."
"3541","On the authority of ʿAmr ibn ʿAbasa al-Sulamī, who said: One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was reviewing horses, and ʿUyayna ibn Ḥiṣn ibn Badr al-Fazārī was with him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: ""I am more knowledgeable about horses than you."" ʿUyayna said: ""And I am more knowledgeable about men than you."" The Prophet ﷺ said to him: ""How so?"" He said: ""The best of men are men who carry their swords on their shoulders, placing their spears on the saddles of their horses, wearing cloaks, from the people of Najd."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""You have lied. Rather, the best of men are the men of the people of Yemen. Faith is Yemeni, extending to Lakhm, Judhām, and ʿĀmila. The consumed of Ḥimyar is better than its consumer, and Ḥaḍramawt is better than Banū al-Ḥārith. Tribe is better than tribe, and tribe is worse than tribe. By Allah! I do not care if the two Ḥāriths both perish. May Allah curse the four kings: Jamdāʾ, Mikhwisāʾ, Mushrakhāʾ, Abḍaʿa, and their sister al-ʿAmarrada."" Then he said: ""My Lord, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me to curse Quraysh twice, so I cursed them; and He commanded me to pray for them, so I prayed for them twice."" Then he said: ""ʿUṣayya disobeyed Allah and His Messenger, except Qays, Jaʿda, and ʿUṣayya."" Then he said: ""Aslam, Ghifār, Muzayna, and their allies from Juhayna are better than Banū Asad, Tamīm, Ghaṭafān, and Hawāzin in the sight of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, on the Day of Resurrection."" Then he said: ""The worst two tribes among the Arabs are Najrān and Banū Taghlib, and the most tribes in Paradise are Madhḥij and Māʾkul."""
"3542","[AI-translation] From Anas, may Allah be pleased with him: That the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, used to say: ""Indeed, the good is the good of the Hereafter,"" or he said: ""O Allah, there is no good except the good of the Hereafter. So forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirun."
"3543","Mahmud ibn Labid reported: When Sa'd the one with kohl was wounded on the day of the Trench, and his condition became serious, they moved him to a woman named Rufaydah, who used to treat the wounded. The Prophet ﷺ, whenever he passed by him, would say: ""How did you spend the evening?"" And when morning came, he would say: ""How did you spend the morning?"" And he would inform him of his condition. Until it was the night in which his people moved him, and his condition worsened, so they carried him to Banu Abd al-Ashhal, to their dwellings. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, as was his custom to ask about him, and they said: ""They have taken him away."" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out, and we went out with him. He hastened his walk until the straps of our sandals broke and our cloaks fell from our necks. His companions complained to him about this: ""O Messenger of Allah! You have exhausted us with walking."" He said: ""I fear that the angels may precede us to him and wash him, just as they washed Hanzalah."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached the house while he was being washed, and his mother was weeping over him, saying:""Woe to your mother, O Sa'd!   His waist-wrapper and his cloak.""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Every wailing woman lies, except the mother of Sa'd."" Then he was carried out. The people—or whoever Allah willed among them—said: ""O Messenger of Allah! We have never carried a dead body lighter upon us than Sa'd."" He said: ""What prevents you from finding him light? Angels have descended in such-and-such numbers."" And he mentioned a great number which I did not memorize. ""They have never descended before their day today; they carried him along with you."""
"3544","[AI-translation] From 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: I was with the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, at Mecca, and we went out in some of its environs, and no mountain nor tree met him except that it was saying: ""Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah."
"3545","[AI-translation] From Anas, raised to the Prophet: Aslam, Ghifar, and men from Muzaynah and Juhaynah are better than the two allies, Ghatafan and Banu 'Amir ibn Sa'sa'ah. He said: So 'Uyaynah ibn Badr said: ""By Allah! For me to be among these in the Fire - meaning Ghatafan and Banu 'Amir - is more beloved to me than to be among these in Paradise."
"3546","[AI-translation] From Anas, raised to the Prophet: The voice of Abu Talhah in the army is better than a troop."
"3547","[AI-translation] Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him: That the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, had his uncle Abu Talib mentioned in his presence, so he said: ""Perhaps my intercession will benefit him on the Day of Resurrection, so he will be placed in a shallow part of the Fire reaching his ankles, causing his brain to boil from it."
"3548","[AI-translation] From Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Seventy thousand angels descended for the death of Sad bin Muadh, who had never trodden the earth before that. And he said: When he was buried: Glory be to Allah! Had anyone escaped the crushing of the grave, Sad would have escaped it. [And he was squeezed a squeeze, then relief was granted to him.]"
"3549","[AI-translation] Rahman bin Abi Said al-Khudri, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""For the Emigrants are pulpits of gold upon which they will sit on the Day of Resurrection, having been saved from the terror."
"3550","On the authority of ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: ""When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken by night to the Farthest Mosque, he awoke and spoke to the people about it. Some of those who had believed in him and accepted him turned back on their heels (apostatized). They went to Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: 'What do you think of your companion? He claims that he was taken by night to Bayt al-Maqdis (Jerusalem).' He said: 'Did he say that?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'If he said that, then he has spoken the truth.' They said: 'Do you believe that he went to Bayt al-Maqdis last night and returned before morning?' He said: 'Yes, indeed I believe him in what is even farther than that; I believe him with the news of the heavens in a single morning or evening.' For that reason, Abū Bakr was named: al-Ṣiddīq (the Truthful) (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
"3551","[AI-translation] From Jabir who said: ""When Jafar returned from Abyssinia, the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, embraced him."
"3552","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah who said: When was revealed: ""When the help of Allah and the victory comes"" (An-Nasr), he said: The people of Yemen have come to you, they have the most tender hearts. Faith is Yemeni, jurisprudence is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni."
"3553","[AI-translation] Ashari, who said: When this verse was revealed: ""O you who believe! Whoever among you turns back from his religion, then Allah will bring a people whom He loves and who love Him"" (Al-Ma'idah: 54), the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, gestured toward Abu Musa with something he had with him and said: ""They are the people of this."
"3554","[AI-translation] From Jabir, marfu': No man who witnessed Badr and Hudaybiyah will enter the Fire."
"3555","Anas ibn Malik was asked about the dyeing of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not have gray hair except a little, but Abu Bakr and Umar after him dyed with henna and katam."" He said: ""Abu Bakr brought his father Abu Quhafa to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of the Conquest of Mecca, carrying him until he placed him before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Abu Bakr: 'If you had left the old man, we would have come to him'—as an honor for Abu Bakr. So he embraced Islam, and his beard and head were like thaghama in whiteness. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Change them and avoid black.'"""
"3556","[AI-translation] From Abu Barzah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, sent a man to a tribe of the Arab tribes for something—he does not know what it was— He said: So they insulted him and beat him, and he complained of that to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, so he said: ""Had you gone to the people of Oman, they would not have insulted you or beaten you."
"3557","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas: Abu Jahl said: ""If I see Muhammad, I will surely step on his neck."" It was said: ""There he is."" He said: ""I do not see him."" The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""Had he done so, the angels would have seized him visibly. And if the Jews wished for death, they would have died."
"3558","[AI-translation] From Musa bin Talha, from his father, who said: On the day of Uhud, an arrow struck me, and I said: ""Ouch!"" The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""Had you said: In the name of Allah, the angels would have carried you away while the people were looking at you."
"3559","[AI-translation] From Aishah who said: Usamah stumbled on the threshold of the door and got a cut on his face. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Remove the harm from him."" But I was squeamish about it, so he started sucking the blood from it and spitting it away from his face. Then he said: ""If Usamah were a girl, I would have clothed him and adorned him with jewelry until I gave him away in marriage."
"3560","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him: We were sitting with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, when Surah Al-Jumu'ah was revealed to him: ""...and others of them who have not yet joined them"" (Al-Jumu'ah: 3). He said: I said: ""Who are these, O Messenger of Allah?"" But he did not answer him until he asked him once, or twice, or three times. He said: And Salman Al-Farisi was among us. He said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, placed his hand on Salman and then said: ""If faith were at the Pleiades, men from among these would attain it."
"3561","[AI-translation] From 'Uqbah bin 'Amir, attributed to the Prophet: ""If there were a prophet after me, it would be 'Umar."
"3562","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr: We were sitting with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, and 'Amr bin Al-'As had gone to put on his clothes to catch up with me. He said while we were with him: ""A cursed man shall surely enter upon you."" By Allah! I remained anxious, looking out for those entering and leaving, until such-and-such entered: Al-Hakam bin Abi Al-'As."
"3563","[AI-translation] From Salman, attributed to the Prophet: ""There is nothing better than a thousand like it except the human being."
"3564","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, attributed to the Prophet: ""No one has a greater favor upon me than Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him; he supported me with his own self and his wealth, and he married his daughter to me."
"3565","'Aqil ibn Abi Talib said: Quraysh came to Abu Talib and said, ""Have you seen Ahmad? He harms us in our gathering place and in our mosque, so forbid him from that."" He said, ""O 'Aqil, bring me Muhammad."" So I went and brought him. He said, ""O son of my brother! Your paternal uncles claim that you harm them in their gathering place and in their mosque, so desist from that."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ glanced with his sight toward the sky (and in another narration: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned his sight toward the sky). He said, ""I am no more able to abandon that for you than you are able to kindle for me a flame from it""—meaning the sun. Abu Talib said, ""My nephew has not lied, so return."""
"3566","On the authority of ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) dispatched an army and appointed ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib over them. He went on the expedition and took a slave girl, so they disapproved of it. Four of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) made a pact, saying: ""If we meet the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family), we will inform him of what ʿAlī did."" It was the custom of the Muslims that when they returned from a journey, they would first go to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family), greet him, and then return to their dwellings. When the expedition returned, they greeted the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family). One of the four stood up and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Did you not see what ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib did, such and such?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) turned away from him. Then the second stood up and said the same as his statement, so he turned away from him. Then the third stood up and said the same as his statement, so he turned away from him. Then the fourth stood up and said the same as they said. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) turned towards them, and anger was recognizable on his face, and he said: ""What do you want from ʿAlī? Indeed, ʿAlī is from me and I am from him, and he is the guardian of every believer after me."""
"3567","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Aishah: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, said: ""Ammar was never given a choice between two matters except that he chose the more correct of the two."
"3568","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas bin Malik: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""No prophet [among the prophets] was believed as I was believed. Indeed, among the prophets are those who were not believed by anyone from their nation except one man."
"3569","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Aishah: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, said: ""A woman is not harmed whether she is accommodated between two houses of the Ansar, or accommodated between her parents."
"3570","[AI-translation] Minhale bin 'Amr, from Ya'la who said: ""I do not think that anyone among the people saw from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, except less than what I saw."" He then mentioned the matter of the boy, the two palm trees, and the matter of the camel, except that he said: ""What is the matter with your camel that it is complaining against you? It claims that you reared it, but when it grew old, you intended to slaughter it."" [Do not slaughter it, but keep it among the camels, so it may be with them.]"
"3571","On the authority of ʿĀʾishah, Mother of the Believers, she said: We, the wives of the Prophet (peace be upon him), were all with him, not one of us remained behind. Then Fāṭimah came walking, and by Allah, her gait did not differ from the gait of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). When he saw her, he welcomed her and said: ""Welcome, my daughter."" Then he seated her on his right or on his left. Then he whispered to her, and she wept bitterly. When he saw her grief, he whispered to her a second time, and she laughed. So I said to her, from among his wives: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) singled you out with the secret from among us, then you weep?"" When the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) stood up, I asked her: ""What did he whisper to you?"" She said: ""I would not disclose the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)."" When the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) passed away, I said to her: ""I adjure you by the right I have over you to tell me."" She said: ""Now, yes."" So she informed me. She said: ""As for when he whispered to me the first time, he informed me: 'Gabriel used to review the Qurʾān with me once every year, and he has reviewed it with me twice this year, and I do not see the term (of my life) except that it has drawn near. So fear Allah and be patient, for I am an excellent predecessor for you.'"" She said: ""So I wept the weeping you saw. When he saw my distress, he whispered to me a second time and said: 'O Fāṭimah! Would it not please you to be the leader of the women of the believers, or the leader of the women of this nation?' [So I laughed the laughter you saw.]"""
"3572","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn 'Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, looked at the Ka'bah and said: ""How great is your sanctity!"" And in another narration: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, looked at the Ka'bah, he said: ""Welcome to you, O House. How great you are, and how great is your sanctity! But the believer has a greater sanctity with Allah than you. Indeed, Allah made one thing sacred from you, but from the believer He made three things sacred: his blood, his wealth, and to think evil of him."
"3573","[AI-translation] Khudri, raised to the Prophet: ""Mu'adh b. Jabal is the most knowledgeable of people concerning the lawful and unlawful of Allah."
"3574","[AI-translation] Narrated from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Ammar is filled with faith to his very marrow."
"3575","[AI-translation] Narrated from 'Abd Allah who said: I was gathering tooth-sticks from the Arak tree for the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family). He said: The people laughed at the thinness of my legs, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""What are you laughing at?"" They said: ""At the thinness of his legs."" He said: ""[By the One in Whose hand is my soul,] they are heavier in the Balance than Uhud."
"3576","[AI-translation] Narrated from Ibn Mas'ud: He was gathering a miswak from the Arak tree, and he was thin-legged, so the wind began to topple him. The people laughed at him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""What are you laughing at?"" They said: ""O Prophet of Allah, at the thinness of his legs."" He said: ""By the One in Whose hand is my soul! They are both heavier in the Balance than Uhud."
"3577","[AI-translation] He (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever harms 'Ali has harmed me."" Narrated from the hadith of ......."
"3578","[AI-translation] Bara' b. 'Azib, raised to the Prophet: ""Whoever loves the Ansar, Allah loves him, and whoever hates the Ansar, Allah hates him."
"3579","[AI-translation] Narrated from Umm Salama, who said: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: ""Whoever loves 'Ali has loved me, and whoever loves me has loved Allah. Whoever hates 'Ali has hated me, and whoever hates me has hated Allah."
"3580","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurayra who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) came out to us with Hasan and Husayn, this one on his shoulder and that one on his shoulder, and he was kissing this one once and kissing that one once, until he reached us. A man said to him: ""O Messenger of Allah! You love them both."" He said: ""Whoever loves them both has loved me, and whoever hates them both has hated me."
"3581","[AI-translation] Narrated from Jabir b. 'Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever frightens the people of Medina, Allah will frighten him."
"3582","[AI-translation] Rahman b. Jabir b. 'Abd Allah from his father: He went out on the day of al-Harra and his foot was struck (by a stone). He said: ""May he perish who frightens the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)!"" I said: ""And who frightens the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)?"" He said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Whoever frightens this tribe of the Ansar has frightened what is between these two,"" meaning his two sides."
"3583","[AI-translation] From Safiyyah bint Abi 'Ubayd that she heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: Whoever among you is able not to die except in Madinah, let him die there, for whoever dies there, intercession will be made for him, or he will be testified for."
"3584","[AI-translation] He said, peace be upon him: Whoever humiliates Quraysh, Allah humiliates him. Narrated from the hadith of......"
"3585","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, marfu': Whoever insults my Companions, upon him be the curse of Allah, the angels, and all of mankind. ( )"
"3586","[AI-translation] From Jabir, marfu': Whoever is pleased to look at a man from the people of Paradise, let him look at al-Husayn bin 'Ali."
"3587","[AI-translation] From 'A'ishah, she said: I was in my house, and the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, and his Companions were in the courtyard, and between me and them was a curtain. Talhah bin 'Ubaydullah approached, so the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Whoever is pleased to look at a man walking upon the earth, having fulfilled his pledge, let him look at Talhah."
"3588","[AI-translation] From Jabir bin 'Abdullah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: Whoever is pleased to look at a martyr walking upon the face of the earth, let him look at Talhah bin 'Ubaydullah."
"3589","[AI-translation] He said, peace be upon him: Whoever I am his master, 'Ali is his master. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him, and show enmity to whoever shows enmity to him. Narrated from the hadith of..... ( )"
"3590","[AI-translation] ) He said, peace be upon him: (""Those who have earned anger"") are the Jews, and (""those who are astray"") are the Christians. Narrated from the hadith of......"
"3591","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, marfu': Sovereignty is in Quraysh, judgeship is in the Ansar, the call to prayer is in the Abyssinians, jurisprudence is in Yemen, and trustworthiness is in al-Azd."
"3592","[AI-translation] From Jarir, marfu': The Emigrants are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter, and the Tulaqa of Quraysh, and the 'Utaqa of Thaqif are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter."
"3593","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, raised to the Prophet: We are the last of the nations and the first to be judged. It will be said: Where is the unlettered nation and its Prophet? So we are the last ones, the first ones."
"3594","[AI-translation] Jafshish al-Kindi who said: I said to the Prophet, peace be upon him: ""From whom are you, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""We are the Banu al-Nadr ibn Kinanah; we do not trace lineage through our mother, nor do we disown our father."
"3595","On the authority of Khālid ibn Maʿdān, from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, that they said to him: ""Tell us about yourself."" He said: ""Yes, I am the supplication of my father Abraham and the glad tidings of Jesus, peace be upon them both. And my mother saw, when she was pregnant with me, that a light came forth from her which illuminated the palaces of Syria. And I was nursed among the Banū Saʿd ibn Bakr. While I was among some lambs of ours, two men came to me wearing white garments, with a golden basin filled with snow. They laid me down, split open my belly, then took out my heart, split it open, and removed a black clot from it, which they threw away. Then they washed my heart and belly with that snow until they had cleansed it, then returned it to its place. Then one of them said to his companion: 'Weigh him against ten of his ummah.' So they weighed me against ten, and I outweighed them. Then he said: 'Weigh him against a hundred of his ummah.' So they weighed me against a hundred, and I outweighed them. Then he said: 'Weigh him against a thousand of his ummah.' So they weighed me against a thousand, and I outweighed them. He said: 'Leave him, for if you weighed him against his entire ummah, he would outweigh them.'"""
"3596","[AI-translation] Samit: It was said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Inform us about yourself."" He said: ""Yes, I am the supplication of Ibrahim, and the last one to give glad tidings of me was 'Isa ibn Maryam, peace be upon him."
"3597","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, and the people were passing by. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, would say: ""O Abu Hurayrah! Who is this?"" I would say: ""So-and-so."" He would say: ""What a good servant of Allah is so-and-so."" And someone would pass by and he would say: ""Who is this, O Abu Hurayrah?"" I would say: ""So-and-so."" He would say: ""What an evil servant of Allah."" Until Khalid ibn al-Walid passed by, and I said: ""This is Khalid ibn al-Walid, O Messenger of Allah!"" He said: ""What a good servant of Allah is Khalid; a sword from the swords of Allah."
"3598","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: What an excellent people are al-Azd; their mouths are pure, their oaths are righteous, their hearts are clean."
"3599","[AI-translation] 'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib, who said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Have you benefited Abu Talib in any way, for he used to protect you and be angry on your behalf?"" He said: ""Yes; he is in a shallow part of the Fire, and were it not for me (i.e., his intercession), he would have been in the lowest depth of the Fire."
"3600","[AI-translation] From Jabir, raised to the Prophet: The people are followers of Quraysh in good and evil."
"3601","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah: The people are followers of Quraysh in this matter; their Muslims are followers of their Muslims, and their disbelievers are followers of their disbelievers."
"3602","[AI-translation] From Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah who said: We were coming with the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, until we arrived at a garden in Banu al-Najjar. And there was a camel in it; no one entered the garden except that it charged at him. They mentioned that to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, so he came to it and called it. It came, dragging its lip on the ground until it knelt before him. He said: ""Bring a halter."" So he haltered it and handed it to its owner. Then he turned and said: ""There is no one between the heaven and the earth except that he knows that I am the Messenger of Allah, except the disobedient among the jinn and humans."
"3603","[AI-translation] From Anas: The people of Yemen came to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, and said: ""Send with us a man to teach us the Sunnah and Islam."" He said: So he took Abu 'Ubaydah by the hand and said: ""This is the trustworthy one of this Ummah."
"3604","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""This righteous man for whom the gates of heaven were opened was subjected to severe hardship, then relief was granted to him."" He meant Sa'd bin Mu'adh."
"3605","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""This righteous man for whom the gates of heaven were opened was subjected to severe hardship, then relief was granted to him."" He meant Sa'd bin Mu'adh."
"3606","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Aisha, the wife of the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family): I was late one night during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) after 'Isha'. When I came, he asked: ""Where were you?"" I replied: ""I was listening to the recitation of a man among your companions. I have never heard a recitation or voice like his from anyone."" She said: He stood up, and I stood with him until he listened to him. Then he turned to me and said: ""This is Salim, the Mawla of Abu Hudhayfah. Praise be to Allah Who has placed in my Ummah someone like this."
"3607","[AI-translation] Narrated Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said to Al-'Abbas: ""This Al-'Abbas bin 'Abdul-Muttalib is the most generous of Quraysh in hand and the best of them in maintaining ties of kinship."
"3608","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Abdullah bin Hantab: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) saw Abu Bakr and 'Umar and said: ""These two are hearing and sight."
"3609","[AI-translation] Narrated Qays bin Abi Hazim: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) and stood before him. He was seized by a trembling out of awe. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Calm down, for I am not a king. I am only the son of a woman who used to eat dried meat."
"3610","[AI-translation] Fajr: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah, when were you written as a Prophet?"" He replied, ""While Adam was between the spirit and the body."
"3611","[AI-translation] Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""By Him in Whose Hand my soul is, no one hates us, the People of the House, except that Allah will admit him into the Fire."
"3612","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""I long to meet my brothers."" His companions said: ""Are we not your brothers?"" He said: ""You are my companions, but my brothers are those who believed in me without having seen me."
"3613","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""I was weighed against a thousand of my Ummah and I outweighed them, so they began to scatter towards me from the pan of the scale."
"3614","Al-Harith ibn Ziyad al-Sa'idi al-Ansari narrated that he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the Day of the Trench while he was accepting allegiance from the people for migration (Hijrah). He said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Accept the allegiance of this man."" He asked: ""And who is this?"" He replied: ""My cousin, Hawt ibn Yazid or Yazid ibn Hawt."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""I will not accept your allegiance, for the people migrate to you, but you do not migrate to them. By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad ﷺ! No man loves the Ansar until he meets Allah, Blessed and Exalted, except that he will meet Allah, Blessed and Exalted, while He loves him. And no man hates the Ansar until he meets Allah, Blessed and Exalted, except that he will meet Allah, Blessed and Exalted, while He hates him."""
"3615","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, sent Muawiyah to write for him. He said: ""He is eating."" Then he sent to him and said: ""He is eating."" The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""May Allah not fill his belly."
"3616","[AI-translation] Yahsabi who said: I heard Muawiyah narrating and he was saying: ""Beware of the ahadith of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, except for a hadith that was during the era of Umar, for Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, used to make the people fearful in Allah, the Mighty and Sublime. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: 'A group from my Ummah will remain manifest upon the truth; those who oppose them will not harm them until the command of Allah comes, while they are manifest upon the people.'"
"3617","[AI-translation] Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, raised to the Prophet: ""A group from my Ummah will remain manifest upon the truth until the Hour is established."
"3618","[AI-translation] From Thawban, raised to the Prophet: ""A group from my Ummah will remain manifest upon the truth; those who forsake them will not harm them until the command of Allah comes, while they are upon that."
"3619","[AI-translation] From Jubair bin Nufair that Salamah bin Nufail informed them that he came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, and said: ""I have tired of horses, thrown down my weapon, and war has laid down its burdens. I said: 'There is no fighting.'"" The Prophet, peace be upon him, said to him: ""Now the fighting has come. A group from my Ummah will remain manifest upon the people. Allah will raise the hearts of people who fight them, and Allah will provide for them from them, until the command of Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, comes, while they are upon that. Verily, the center of the believers' abode is Al-Sham, and good is tied in the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection."
"3620","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, raised to the Prophet: ""A group from my Ummah will remain steadfast upon the command of Allah; those who oppose them will not harm them."
"3621","[AI-translation] From Zaid bin Arqam that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""A group from my Ummah will continue to fight upon the truth until the command of Allah comes, and I see you as them, O people of Al-Sham."
"3622","[AI-translation] From Imran bin Husain, raised to the Prophet: ""A group from my Ummah will continue to fight upon the truth, manifest against those who are hostile to them, until the last of them fights the False Messiah."
"3623","[AI-translation] From Jabir bin Abdullah, raised to the Prophet: ""A group from my Ummah will continue to fight upon the truth, manifest, until the Day of Resurrection."" He said: ""Then Isa, son of Maryam, peace be upon him and his family, descends. Their leader will say: 'Come! Lead us in prayer.' He will say: 'No, some of you are leaders over others, as an honor from Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, to this Ummah.'"
"3624","On the authority of ʿUmayr ibn al-Aswad and Kathīr ibn Murrah al-Ḥaḍramī, they said: Abū Hurayrah and Ibn al-Ṣamt used to say: ""The Muslims will not cease to be in the land until the Hour is established."" And that is because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""There will not cease to be from my Ummah a group standing firm upon the command of Allah, Mighty and Majestic; those who oppose them will not harm them. They fight their enemies. Whenever one war ends, the war of another people breaks out. Allah causes the hearts of a people to deviate so that He may provide for them (the steadfast group) from it, until the Hour comes upon them like a piece of the dark night, so they are terrified by it, until they don for it coats of mail."" And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""They are the people of Shām."" And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pointed with his finger toward Shām until it became sore."
"3625","[AI-translation] Asqa who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""You will remain in good as long as there is among you someone who saw me and accompanied me. By Allah! You will remain in good as long as there is among you someone who saw someone who saw me and accompanied someone who accompanied me. By Allah! You will remain in good as long as there is among you someone who saw someone who saw someone who saw me, and accompanied someone who accompanied someone who accompanied me."
"3626","[AI-translation] From Aishah, marfu': Do not insult Waraqah, for I saw for him a Paradise or two Paradises."
"3627","[AI-translation] Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, was at al-Hudaybiyah and said: ""Do not light a fire at night."" Then afterwards he said: ""Light and prepare [food], for indeed no people after you will attain your sa' and your mudd."
"3628","[AI-translation] From Nu'aym ibn Dijajah that he said: Abu Mas'ud 'Uqbah ibn 'Amr al-Ansari entered upon 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, and 'Ali said to him: ""Are you the one who says that a hundred years will not pass over the people while an eye blinks on the earth? Rather, the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: 'A hundred years will not pass over the people while an eye blinks on the earth from those who are alive today.' By Allah, the hope of this Ummah is after a hundred years."
"3629","[AI-translation] From Aishah, marfu': Do not insult Waraqah, for I saw for him a Paradise or two Paradises."
"3630","[AI-translation] Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, marfu': A group of my Ummah will continue to prevail until the Command of Allah comes to them while they are prevailing."
"3631","[AI-translation] From Jabir who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: ""It is not lawful for anyone to carry weapons in it for fighting."" Meaning al-Madinah."
"3632","[AI-translation] From Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, marfu': The people of the West will continue to prevail until the Hour is established."
"3633","ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir said: ""I and ʿAlī were companions on the expedition of Dhāt al-ʿUshayrah. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ alighted there and stayed, we saw some people of Banū Mudlij working at a well of theirs among palm trees. ʿAlī said to me: 'O Abū al-Yaqẓān! Would you like to go to these people and watch how they work?' So we went to them and watched their work for a while. Then sleep overcame us, so I and ʿAlī went and lay down in a hollow among the palm trees on dusty ground, and we fell asleep. By Allah! Nothing woke us except the Messenger of Allah ﷺ nudging us with his foot, and we had become covered in dust from that dusty ground. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Abū Turāb!' — because of the dust seen on him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Shall I not tell you of the two most wretched of people?' We said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Uḥaymir Thamūd, who hamstrung the she-camel, and the one who will strike you, O ʿAlī, on this' — meaning the crown of ʿAlī's head — 'until this is soaked with blood' — meaning his beard."""
"3634","Abu Hurairah narrated: I came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) with some dates and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Invoke Allah for blessing in them."" So he gathered them (and in another narration: he arranged them before him), then he invoked blessing for me in them. He said to me: ""O Abu Hurairah! Take them and put them in this pouch of yours, or in this pouch. Whenever you want to take something from it, put your hand in it and take it, but do not scatter them. For I have carried from this date [produce] such-and-such wasq (and in another narration: fifty wasq) in the cause of Allah. So we used to eat from it and feed others. And it did not leave my waist until the day Uthman was killed, whereupon it was cut off (from my waist and fell)."
"3635","Abu al-Darda' (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Abu Bakr approached, holding the edge of his garment until his knee was exposed. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""As for your companion, he has taken a risk."" He greeted and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! There was something between me and Ibn al-Khattab, so I hurried to him, then I regretted it, so I asked him to forgive me, but he refused, so I came to you."" He said: ""May Allah forgive you, O Abu Bakr"" (three times). Then Umar regretted it, so he went to Abu Bakr's house and asked: ""Is Abu Bakr there?"" They said: ""No."" So he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and greeted. The face of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry until Abu Bakr felt compassion, so he knelt on his knees and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! By Allah! I was the more unjust"" (twice). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O people! Allah sent me to you, and you said: 'You lie,' and Abu Bakr said: 'You speak the truth,' and he supported me with his self and wealth. Will you not leave my companion for me?"" (twice). So he was not harmed after that."
"3636","[AI-translation] From Abu Salih, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""O people! I am but a gifted mercy."
"3637","[AI-translation] From Anas ibn Malik that a man said: ""O Muhammad! O our master and son of our master! The best of us and son of the best of us!"" So the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""O people! Hold fast to your piety, and let not Satan delude you."" (In a narration: ""Speak your words, and let not Satan drag you). ""I am Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah, the servant of Allah and His Messenger. By Allah! I do not love that you elevate me above the rank which Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, has placed me."
"3638","[AI-translation] From Yahya ibn Sa'id, who said: We were with 'Ali ibn al-Husayn when a group of people from al-Kufah came, so 'Ali said: ""O people of Iraq! Love us with the love of Islam. I heard my father say: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: 'O people! Do not elevate me above my worth, for Allah took me as a servant before He took me as a prophet.'"" I mentioned it to Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, and he said: ""And after He took him as a prophet."
"3639","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah that Abu Hind cupped the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) at the crown of his head, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: O Banu Bayadah! Marry off Abu Hind and marry off to him. And he was a cupper."
"3640","[AI-translation] Rahman bin 'Awf that he heard Hassan bin Thabit al-Ansari asking Abu Hurayrah to testify: I adjure you by Allah, did you hear the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) say: O Hassan! Answer on behalf of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family), O Allah, support him with the Holy Spirit? Abu Hurayrah said: Yes."
"3641","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar, who said: There was a greenishness in Safiyyah's eye, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) said to her: What is this greenishness in your eye? She said: I said to my husband: I saw in a dream a moon falling in my lap, so he slapped me and said: Do you want the king of Yathrib? She said: And there was none more hateful to me than the Messenger of Allah, who killed my father and my husband. So he continued to apologize to me, saying: O Safiyyah! Your father incited the Arabs against [us], and did such and such... He apologized to her. (She said) until that departed from my heart."
"3642","[AI-translation] From Qays who said: I heard Jarir saying: The Messenger of Allah never saw me since I embraced Islam except that he smiled in my face. And the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: A man from the best of the people of Yemen will enter through this door, upon his face is the trace of an angel. Then Jarir entered."
"3643","[AI-translation] From Muhammad bin Jubayr bin Mut'im from his father who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) on the road to Makkah, he said: The people of Yemen will appear to you as if they are clouds; they are the best of the people on the earth. A man from the Ansar said: Are not we [too], O Messenger of Allah? He remained silent. He said: Are not we [too], O Messenger of Allah? He remained silent. He said: Are not we [too], O Messenger of Allah? He said in the third time a weak word: Except you."
"3644","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah bin Busr, that the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) said to him: This boy will live a century. He said: And he lived a hundred years."
